window.PPL_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"path":"product-research/product-research.html","anchor":"start","page":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"title":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"text":{"en":"Draft 0.1 Product Research Find the evidence that changes the next product decision. Research starts with a consequential question.","zh":"初稿 0.1 产品研究 找到能改变下一步产品决定的证据。 研究从一个会影响行动的问题开始。"}},{"path":"product-research/product-research.html","anchor":"questions","page":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"title":{"en":"Start from the decision","zh":"从决策开始"},"text":{"en":"Start from the decision Research is useful when its findings can change an action: whom to serve, which problem to prioritize, which alternative to compare, or which assumption to test. Decision What action may change? Uncertainty What must we learn? Evidence What can answer it? Next action Proceed, narrow, test, or pause. Research brief Name the user, task, decision, deadline, and current alternative. Turn opinions into questions that evidence can answer. Assumption priority Investigate assumptions with high consequence and weak evidence first. Set a time and cost boundary before collecting more material. Example · turn a feature request into a research question “Add an AI reply button” is a proposed solution. Ask where support staff spend effort today, which replies require judgment, and what prevents a draft from being sent. Those answers may support drafting, better source retrieval, or a review queue.","zh":"从决策开始 研究的价值在于发现能改变行动：服务谁、优先解决什么、比较哪个替代方案，或先验证哪个假设。 决策 什么行动可能改变？ 不确定性 需要知道什么？ 证据 什么证据能回答？ 下一步 推进、收窄、验证或暂停。 研究简报 写清用户、任务、决策、时间与当前替代方案。把观点转成证据可以回答的问题。 假设优先级 优先研究后果重大、证据薄弱的假设。收集更多资料前，先确定时间与成本边界。 示例 · 把功能请求转成研究问题 “增加 AI 回复按钮”是方案。可以先研究客服目前把时间花在哪里、哪些回复需要判断，以及什么原因让草稿无法直接发送。答案可能支持自动起草，也可能更需要资料检索或审核队列。"}},{"path":"product-research/product-research.html","anchor":"methods","page":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"title":{"en":"Choose the evidence approach","zh":"选择研究方式"},"text":{"en":"Choose the evidence approach Choose methods for the uncertainty and population. Several methods can contribute to one decision, with different limits on what they establish. Question Approach What to watch How is the task actually done? Interviews, contextual observation, task artifacts, support cases. Understand context and workarounds; separate what people say from what they do. What alternatives exist? Desk research, primary documentation, comparable product walkthroughs. Record capability, version, effort, and limits; verify material claims. Where and how often does friction occur? Validated analytics, segmentation, appropriately sampled surveys. Define the denominator, window, sample, and missing populations. Can this capability work? API contracts, provider documentation, approved spike or eval. Feasibility evidence supports a bounded capability claim; demand needs its own evidence. Did the change cause improvement? Controlled experiments or a defensible causal design. Use the analytics and experiments practice for design and interpretation. Planning participant research · sample, consent, and neutral questions Recruit for the task and relevant differences in expertise, context, accessibility, and risk. Make selection bias explicit. Ask about recent real behavior and artifacts before presenting a solution. Use open questions and neutral tasks. Define consent, recording, access, redaction, and retention. Participant contact requires explicit authorization. Choose sample size and additional rounds for the method, variation, and decision risk; report coverage limitations.","zh":"选择研究方式 根据问题与目标人群选择方法。一个决策可以组合多种方法，但每种证据能说明的范围不同。 需要回答什么 可用方式 注意什么 任务实际如何完成？ 访谈、情境观察、任务产物、支持记录。 理解上下文与替代做法，区分用户描述与实际行为。 有什么替代方案？ 案头研究、第一方文档、同任务产品走查。 记录能力、版本、投入与限制，核实重要声明。 阻力出现在哪里、频率如何？ 经过验证的分析数据、分群、采样合理的问卷。 明确分母、时间窗口、样本与未覆盖人群。 这项能力是否可行？ API 契约、供应商文档、获批的小型技术验证或 eval。 可行性证据说明特定条件下的能力；需求价值需要另外的证据。 改动是否造成改善？ 受控实验或有依据的因果分析设计。 使用产品分析与实验实践设计和解读。 规划参与者研究 · 样本、同意与中立提问 围绕任务与经验、情境、无障碍需求和风险差异选择参与者，说明样本偏差。 介绍方案前，先了解近期真实行为与产物。采用开放提问和中立任务。 明确知情同意、录音、访问、脱敏与保留规则。联系参与者需要明确授权。 根据方法、差异与决策风险确定样本和追加轮次，说明覆盖限制。"}},{"path":"product-research/product-research.html","anchor":"system-probing","page":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"title":{"en":"Product System Probing","zh":"产品系统探查"},"text":{"en":"Behavioral research method Product System Probing Build a working model of how a partially observable product behaves through realistic interaction—without turning every research question into a full evaluation program. Learn through the smallest useful probe Start from a user job Use a realistic outcome and consequential decision. Observe the trajectory Capture interpretation, questions, assumptions, recommendations and action gates across turns. Form competing hypotheses Keep observable behavior separate from system inference and architecture guesses. Change one meaningful variable Choose a probe that makes the hypotheses predict different behavior. Update the model Record the boundary, remaining uncertainty and highest-information next step. Use it when You can interact with a product but cannot yet inspect its full implementation, data or internal decision path. It produces An evidence-linked behavioral product model—not a benchmark score or a claim that the internal architecture has been proven. User job & value path Where does value begin, and what remains with the user? Interaction trajectory How does intent become clarification, diagnosis, recommendation and follow-up? Domain capability Which domain relationships can the product apply to a decision? Agency & orchestration When does it ask, investigate, invoke, recommend, wait or act? Context & state Which goals, corrections and assumptions remain behaviorally active? Integration boundary What works from knowledge, supplied context, connected retrieval and action permission? Execution Who operates Use it when Plan only No interaction in this turn You need scenarios, hypotheses, probes, evidence capture and stopping rules before access is available. Human-guided The user operates; the agent adapts The target is unavailable to tools or every interaction needs human control. Agent-operated The agent uses browser or computer tools A public, demo or authorized test surface supports bounded, non-destructive interaction. Hybrid The agent proceeds; the user handles gates The agent can research autonomously but login, MFA, CAPTCHA, consent or account connection needs the user. Probe types · choose by the current uncertainty Baseline Run the realistic task naturally. Follow-up Continue the same problem across turns. Perturbation Change one meaningful variable. Context Observe whether earlier information stays active. Conflict Introduce competing goals or sources. Boundary Find where behavior changes form or stops. Recovery Correct an assumption and observe real revision. Transfer Try a structurally similar task. Integration Compare supplied context with connected retrieval or action. Evidence boundary · do not turn behavior into architecture DECLARED The product or documentation says it. OBSERVATION It was directly visible under recorded conditions. BEHAVIORAL INFERENCE A bounded explanation fits the observations. IMPLEMENTATION HYPOTHESIS A possible internal mechanism remains unverified. VERIFIED An authoritative internal source corroborates it. Open the complete probing workflow → Use the behavioral model template →","zh":"行为研究方法 产品系统探查 通过真实交互，逐步建立对部分可观察产品如何运作的工作模型，而不把每个研究问题都扩张成完整评估体系。 用最小且有效的 probe 学习 从用户任务开始 使用真实目标与会影响行动的决定。 观察交互轨迹 记录多轮中的理解、提问、假设、建议与行动关口。 形成竞争假设 把可观察行为、系统推断与架构猜测分开。 只改变一个关键变量 选择能让不同假设产生不同预测的 probe。 更新行为模型 记录边界、剩余不确定性与信息量最高的下一步。 适用于 你可以与产品交互，但还不能完整查看实现、数据或内部决策链路。 它产出 一份可追溯证据的产品行为模型，而不是 benchmark 分数，也不声称已经证明内部架构。 用户任务与价值路径 价值从哪里出现，哪些工作仍由用户完成？ 交互轨迹 意图如何经过澄清、诊断、建议与后续行动？ 领域能力 产品能把哪些领域关系应用到决策中？ 自主性与编排 它何时提问、调查、调用、建议、等待或行动？ 上下文与状态 哪些目标、纠正与假设仍然影响后续行为？ 集成边界 知识、手动信息、连接检索与行动权限分别支持什么？ 执行方式 谁来操作 适用情况 只做规划 本轮不进行产品交互 访问条件尚未具备，先设计场景、假设、probe、证据记录与停止条件。 人工操作、Agent 引导 用户操作，Agent 动态调整 工具无法访问目标，或每一步都需要人工控制。 Agent 直接操作 Agent 使用浏览器或 computer-use 工具 公开、演示或获授权的测试环境允许有限、非破坏性交互。 混合执行 Agent 推进，用户处理人工关口 Agent 可自主研究，但登录、MFA、CAPTCHA、同意或账号连接需要用户完成。 Probe 类型 · 根据当前不确定性选择 Baseline 自然执行真实任务。 Follow-up 在多轮中继续同一问题。 Perturbation 改变一个关键变量。 Context 观察早先信息是否持续生效。 Conflict 引入冲突目标或来源。 Boundary 寻找行为改变形式或停止的位置。 Recovery 纠正假设并观察是否真正修正。 Transfer 尝试结构相似的任务。 Integration 比较手动信息、连接检索与授权行动。 证据边界 · 不要把行为直接写成架构 DECLARED 产品或文档这样声明。 OBSERVATION 在已记录条件下直接观察到。 BEHAVIORAL INFERENCE 一个有边界的解释符合现有观察。 IMPLEMENTATION HYPOTHESIS 可能的内部机制仍未验证。 VERIFIED 权威内部来源已经确认。 打开完整探查工作流 → 使用行为模型模板 →"}},{"path":"product-research/product-research.html","anchor":"synthesis","page":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"title":{"en":"Turn sources into findings","zh":"从来源形成判断"},"text":{"en":"Turn sources into findings Keep the observation separate from your interpretation. A team should be able to trace each recommendation back to what was actually learned. Source Document, interview, behavior, or runtime. Observation What was said or seen. Interpretation Pattern and alternative explanations. Implication What changes in the decision. Finding record Purpose Example field Evidence and scope Let others verify the claim and its population. Source ID, link, date/version, method, population. Interpretation and uncertainty Keep hypotheses reviewable instead of presenting them as observed facts. Pattern, contradictory cases, confidence, missing evidence. Decision implication Make research actionable. Affected assumption, recommended action, decision owner. Quality checks · contradictions, freshness, and claims Preserve conflicting reports and abandoned tasks. A minority pattern may identify a high-risk segment. Count independent evidence, not copied claims repeated across websites. Check product version and regional availability. A mention count is not prevalence without a sampling basis; an observed association does not establish causation. Mark inaccessible sources and missing observations as unverified. AI-generated examples illustrate a method; they are not research participants.","zh":"从来源形成判断 把观察与解释分开。团队应该能够沿每条建议追溯到实际获得的证据。 来源 文档、访谈、行为或运行记录。 观察 直接说了什么、看到了什么。 解释 模式与其他可能解释。 影响 哪项决定因此改变。 发现记录 用途 记录内容 证据与范围 让他人核实结论及其适用人群。 来源编号、链接、日期或版本、方法与人群。 解释与不确定性 让推断可讨论，不混作观察事实。 模式、反例、可信度与缺失证据。 对决策的影响 让研究能够改变行动。 受影响假设、建议行动与决策负责人。 质量检查 · 矛盾、时效与结论边界 保留矛盾报告与放弃的任务。少数案例可能揭示高风险群体。 区分独立证据与多网站转载的同一声明，核对产品版本和地区可用性。 提及次数没有采样依据时不能代表普遍程度；观察到的关联不能直接证明因果。 无法访问的来源与缺失观察标为未验证。AI 生成例子可说明方法，但不是参与者证据。"}},{"path":"product-research/product-research.html","anchor":"collaboration","page":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"title":{"en":"Work with an agent","zh":"与 Agent 配合"},"text":{"en":"Work with an agent Automate source organization and first-pass synthesis, while preserving human responsibility for participant relationships and consequential choices. Agent prepares and checks Inspect context, choose a research route, collect authorized evidence, compare alternatives, surface contradictions, and draft an evidence-linked recommendation. People decide and validate Confirm the decision and acceptable risk, authorize participant work, review ambiguous interpretations, and decide what action the findings justify. A useful research handoff Return the recommendation, strongest findings, limitations, and the next question. Keep a linked evidence appendix for deeper review. Stop when the next decision is adequately supported or the approved budget is reached; retain unresolved uncertainty.","zh":"与 Agent 配合 让 Agent 整理来源并做初步归纳，同时保留人对参与者关系和重要决定的责任。 Agent 准备与检查 检查上下文、选择研究路径、收集授权证据、比较替代方案、指出矛盾，形成带证据的建议。 人判断与验证 确认决策与可接受风险、授权参与者研究、审阅有歧义的解释，并决定发现足以支持什么行动。 有用的研究交接 交付建议、最重要的发现、局限与下一问题，详细证据放在可追溯的附录。证据足以支持下一决定，或达到批准预算时收束，并保留未解决的不确定性。"}},{"path":"product-research/product-research.html","anchor":"files","page":{"en":"Product Research","zh":"产品研究"},"title":{"en":"Files and references","zh":"文件结构与参考"},"text":{"en":"Files and references File relationships for this module. Use the workflow sections above for the practical steps. Internal files View this folder on GitHub ↗ Entry README.md Shared file dependencies Task and authority ../_shared/task-contract.md Workflow branches Research workflow 01-product-research.prompt.md Product System Probing 02-product-system-probing.prompt.md Supporting files · read when needed Behavioral product model template templates/behavioral-product-model.md Use for a durable evidence ledger, hypotheses, boundaries and next probes. Shared restructuring method ( EN / 简中 ) ../product-ux-rethinking/00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md For deeper evidence, responsibility or structural questions. Product framing ../product-ux-rethinking/README.md When findings are ready to inform what to build. Testing and eval ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md For concrete quality, reliability or comparative measurement. Analytics and experiments ../product-analytics-experimentation/README.md For behavior or causal-impact questions. Context update discipline ../context-update-discipline/README.md When feedback changes the current scope or intent. Mermaid file map ↗ How the agent reads these files Choose the standard research workflow for planning, sources or synthesis, or Product System Probing for behavioral learning through realistic interaction. Read both only for an explicit combined request. This package currently starts from the README you give the agent. An installed skill is discovered through its name and description, then its SKILL.md is loaded; references and scripts support the selected task. These maps describe intended reading routes, not a live execution trace or an access-control mechanism. Official skill documentation ↗ External references GOV.UK · Research planning Question-led methods and participant planning.","zh":"文件结构与参考 本模块的文件关系。具体做法见上方工作流内容。 内部文件 在 GitHub 查看本模块文件夹 ↗ 入口 README.md 共用文件 任务与操作边界 ../_shared/task-contract.md 工作流分支 研究工作流 01-product-research.prompt.md 产品系统探查 02-product-system-probing.prompt.md 支持文件 · 按需读取 产品行为模型模板 templates/behavioral-product-model.md 用于持续记录证据、假设、边界与下一项 probe。 通用重构方法 ( EN / 简中 ) ../product-ux-rethinking/00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md 需要深入处理证据、责任或结构问题时读取。 产品定义 ../product-ux-rethinking/README.md 研究结论需要转成产品方案时读取。 测试与评估 ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md 需要具体质量、可靠性或对照衡量方案时读取。 产品分析与实验 ../product-analytics-experimentation/README.md 涉及用户行为或因果影响时读取。 上下文更新规范 ../context-update-discipline/README.md 反馈改变当前范围或意图时读取。 查看 Mermaid 文件图 ↗ Agent 如何读取这些文件 研究规划、来源调查或归纳使用标准研究工作流；通过真实交互理解产品行为时使用 Product System Probing。只有明确的组合任务才读取两者。 当前 package 从你交给 Agent 的 README 开始。已安装的 skill 会先通过名称和描述被发现，再读取 SKILL.md，并按任务使用参考文件或脚本。这张图说明预期读取路线，不是实际执行轨迹，也不是权限控制。 官方 skill 说明 ↗ 外部参考 GOV.UK · 研究规划 问题导向的方法选择与参与者规划。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/product-framing.html","anchor":"start","page":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"title":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"text":{"en":"Draft 0.1 Product Framing Define what the feature should become, before committing to its implementation. A useful product model connects the user outcome, responsibility, and evidence.","zh":"初稿 0.1 产品定义 在投入实现前，定义功能应该成为什么。 有用的产品模型，把用户结果、责任与证据连在一起。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/product-framing.html","anchor":"problem","page":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"title":{"en":"Define the problem and outcome","zh":"定义问题与结果"},"text":{"en":"Define the problem and outcome Start with the job people need to complete and their current alternative. A feature idea becomes a product direction only when its value, responsibility, and evidence are clear. User job Trigger, context, current workaround. Outcome Observable completion and quality. Product model Objects, responsibility, lifecycle. Useful MVP A bounded value hypothesis to test. Define Why it matters What to write Problem evidence Shows whom the problem affects and why it is worth solving. Users, context, frequency/severity evidence, alternatives, open assumptions. Success Makes a direction testable. Completed user job, quality bar, user effort, operating limits. Boundary Clarifies what the first version is responsible for. Core job, adjacent products, required safety, future capabilities. When evidence is weak State a working hypothesis and the check that could disprove it. Explore concepts as proposals, then test the most consequential assumption before investing in implementation. Existing prototype code is feasibility evidence.","zh":"定义问题与结果 先理解用户要完成的任务与当前替代做法。明确价值、责任和证据后，功能想法才成为可判断的产品方向。 用户任务 触发、情境与当前替代做法。 结果 可观察的完成与质量。 产品模型 对象、责任与生命周期。 有用的 MVP 用有限范围验证价值假设。 需要定义 为什么重要 写清什么 问题证据 说明问题影响谁、为什么值得解决。 用户、情境、频率或严重程度证据、替代方案与未验证假设。 成功标准 让方向可以验证。 完成的用户任务、质量标准、用户投入与运行限制。 产品边界 明确首版负责解决什么。 核心任务、相邻产品、必要安全要求与未来能力。 证据不足时如何继续 明确工作假设及可能推翻它的验证方式。概念探索保持提案状态，大规模实现前先验证后果最重的假设。已有原型代码可以作为可行性证据。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/product-framing.html","anchor":"concepts","page":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"title":{"en":"Compare product concepts","zh":"比较产品概念"},"text":{"en":"Compare product concepts Compare how the product creates value and allocates responsibility. Use the same user job and quality bar for each concept. Concept direction Interaction and responsibility Evidence needed Assisted workspace The user creates and edits with context-aware help. Does assistance reduce effort while preserving useful control? Review queue The system prepares candidates; the user focuses on exceptions and approval. Are drafts reliable enough, and can reviewers detect consequential errors? Bounded automation The system executes eligible low-risk work within explicit authority. Are permission, readiness, quality, recovery, and oversight sufficient? Illustrative models These are examples of structurally different approaches, not a required roadmap. Include the current manual or non-AI alternative; recommend the concept that best fits the task, maturity, and evidence. Concept comparison checklist Define the mental model, core objects, entry point, primary flow, and completion state. Compare user effort, output quality, trust, authority, recovery, feasibility, and operating cost. Name the highest-risk assumption and what evidence would favor or reject each concept. Produce mockup variations only when interaction or information architecture remains meaningfully unresolved.","zh":"比较产品概念 比较产品如何创造价值、如何分配责任。每个概念使用相同的用户任务与质量标准。 概念方向 交互与责任 需要什么证据 辅助工作区 用户在上下文辅助下创建与修改。 辅助是否降低投入，同时保留有用的控制？ 审核队列 系统准备候选结果，用户集中处理例外与批准。 草稿是否足够可靠，审核者能否发现重要错误？ 有边界的自动化 系统在明确权限内执行符合条件的低风险任务。 权限、就绪条件、质量、恢复与监督是否充分？ 示意模型 这些是结构不同的方向示例，不是必经路线。把当前人工或非 AI 做法纳入比较，推荐最符合任务、成熟度和证据的概念。 概念比较检查项 定义心智模型、核心对象、入口、主流程与完成状态。 比较用户投入、输出质量、信任、权限、恢复、可行性与运行成本。 指出每个概念的高风险假设，以及支持或否定它的证据。 交互或信息架构仍有实质分歧时，再制作 mockup variations。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/product-framing.html","anchor":"responsibility","page":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"title":{"en":"Allocate system and human responsibility","zh":"分配系统与人的责任"},"text":{"en":"Allocate system and human responsibility A product model explains what the system resolves, what it recommends, and which consequential decisions remain with people. Responsibility System role Human boundary Context and understanding Gather permitted sources; check scope, freshness, gaps, and conflicts. Confirm goals, preferences, and material unknowns. Generate and recommend Produce grounded candidates, validate rules, and explain trade-offs. Choose consequential trade-offs and correct unsupported assumptions. Execute Act only within explicit permission and verified readiness. Approve material actions and control overrides. Recover Retry safely, reconcile ambiguous outcomes, and preserve progress. Choose alternatives when recovery changes the intended outcome. AI capability specification Required context, provenance, tenant scope, freshness, and memory ownership. Model/tool capability, uncertainty, output contract, and deterministic validation. Draft, recommendation, approval, execution, and read-back as distinct states. Quality and safety evidence required before expanding autonomy.","zh":"分配系统与人的责任 产品模型需要说明：系统直接解决什么、建议什么，以及哪些重要决定保留给人。 责任 系统负责 人的边界 上下文与理解 汇集允许使用的来源，检查范围、时效、缺失与冲突。 确认目标、偏好与重要未知信息。 生成与建议 生成有依据的候选，验证规则并解释取舍。 决定重要取舍，纠正无依据的假设。 执行 只在明确权限与已验证就绪条件内执行。 批准重要行动并控制覆盖操作。 恢复 安全重试、核对不明确结果并保留进度。 恢复方案改变预期结果时，决定是否采用。 AI 能力需要写清什么 所需上下文、来源、租户范围、时效与记忆管理责任。 模型与工具能力、不确定性、输出契约和确定性验证。 区分草稿、建议、批准、执行与回读验证状态。 扩大自主执行前需要的质量与安全证据。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/product-framing.html","anchor":"lifecycle","page":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"title":{"en":"Write the lifecycle before the screens","zh":"先写生命周期，再设计页面"},"text":{"en":"Write the lifecycle before the screens Name the objects and states that persist across visits. Walk through a realistic task, including waiting, leaving, returning, and recovery. Understand Sources and goal are available. Prepare A versioned result can be reviewed. Decide Authority and consequences are clear. Act and verify Persist or execute; confirm actual state. Text-flow contract · one row per meaningful step Question Required answer What does the user see and decide? Task, primary message, action, supporting evidence, advanced details. What does the system resolve? Inputs, source of truth, validation, permission, and state change. How does recovery work? Empty, stale, partial, failed, duplicate, interrupted, or ambiguous cases.","zh":"先写生命周期，再设计页面 定义跨访问保留的对象与状态。用真实任务走完等待、离开、返回与恢复，验证体验是否连贯。 理解 来源与目标明确。 准备 结果有版本、可审阅。 决定 权限与后果清晰。 行动与验证 保存或执行，确认真实状态。 文字 flow 契约 · 每个关键步骤写一行 问题 需要回答 用户看到什么、决定什么？ 任务、主要信息、操作、依据与进阶详情。 系统解决什么？ 输入、权威来源、校验、权限与状态变化。 如何恢复？ 空、过期、部分成功、失败、重复、中断或结果不明确的情况。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/product-framing.html","anchor":"mvp","page":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"title":{"en":"Scope the first useful version","zh":"确定首个有用版本"},"text":{"en":"Scope the first useful version Separate the user promise from its implementation dependencies. Keep the smallest end-to-end scope that can deliver the outcome safely. Horizon Product and design Engineering and evidence V1 · Useful and safe Core task, decision ownership, necessary states, clear content, recovery. Real contracts/data, critical validation, bounded execution, one verified slice. Next · Evidence-led expansion Advanced controls, additional tasks, personalization where justified. Scale, deeper integration, automation, and optimization after gates pass. Approval-ready output Return the recommended concept, evidence and assumptions, lifecycle, responsibility map, MVP boundary, highest-risk validation, and proposal ID. The agent stops at the authorized phase and asks for the next specific approval.","zh":"确定首个有用版本 把用户承诺与实现依赖分开。选择能够安全交付结果的最小端到端范围。 阶段 产品与设计 工程与证据 V1 · 有用且安全 核心任务、决策责任、必要状态、清晰内容与恢复。 真实契约与数据、关键验证、有边界的执行，以及一条已验证路径。 后续 · 按证据扩展 有依据的高级控制、更多任务与个性化。 通过门槛后再扩展规模、集成、自动化与优化。 可供批准的产出 交付推荐概念、证据与假设、生命周期、责任图、MVP 边界、最高风险验证和提案编号。Agent 在授权阶段结束，并请求下一阶段的明确批准。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/product-framing.html","anchor":"files","page":{"en":"Product Framing","zh":"产品定义"},"title":{"en":"Files and references","zh":"文件结构与参考"},"text":{"en":"Files and references File relationships for this module. Use the workflow sections above for the practical steps. Internal files View this folder on GitHub ↗ Entry README.md Shared file dependencies Task and authority ../_shared/task-contract.md Shared restructuring method ( EN / 简中 ) 00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md Workflow branches Plan a new feature ( EN / 简中 ) 02-new-feature-product-planning.en.md Rethink an existing MVP ( EN / 简中 ) 01-existing-mvp-ux-reimagination.en.md Supporting files · read when needed Product research ../product-research/README.md For unresolved user, alternative or feasibility questions. AI system audit ../ai-product-system-audit/README.md For material wiring, harness or contract uncertainty. Testing and eval ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md For concrete quality, reliability or comparative measurement. Delivery and learning ../delivery-learning/README.md For an approved implementation scope. Context update discipline ../context-update-discipline/README.md When feedback changes the current scope or intent. Mermaid file map ↗ How the agent reads these files This page starts with new-feature planning. Use the MVP route only if the task includes rethinking an existing implementation. Read one language version. This package currently starts from the README you give the agent. An installed skill is discovered through its name and description, then its SKILL.md is loaded; references and scripts support the selected task. These maps describe intended reading routes, not a live execution trace or an access-control mechanism. Official skill documentation ↗ External references Design Council · Double Diamond Problem discovery and exploration of distinct solutions.","zh":"文件结构与参考 本模块的文件关系。具体做法见上方工作流内容。 内部文件 在 GitHub 查看本模块文件夹 ↗ 入口 README.md 共用文件 任务与操作边界 ../_shared/task-contract.md 通用重构方法 ( EN / 简中 ) 00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md 工作流分支 规划新功能 ( EN / 简中 ) 02-new-feature-product-planning.en.md 重新构想已有 MVP ( EN / 简中 ) 01-existing-mvp-ux-reimagination.en.md 支持文件 · 按需读取 产品研究 ../product-research/README.md 用户、替代方案或可行性仍需研究时读取。 AI 系统审查 ../ai-product-system-audit/README.md 接入、harness 或契约存在关键不确定性时读取。 测试与评估 ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md 需要具体质量、可靠性或对照衡量方案时读取。 交付与复盘 ../delivery-learning/README.md 进入已批准的实施范围时读取。 上下文更新规范 ../context-update-discipline/README.md 反馈改变当前范围或意图时读取。 查看 Mermaid 文件图 ↗ Agent 如何读取这些文件 本页以新功能规划为起点；任务涉及已有实现重构时才转向 MVP 路线。每份工作流选择一种语言版本。 当前 package 从你交给 Agent 的 README 开始。已安装的 skill 会先通过名称和描述被发现，再读取 SKILL.md，并按任务使用参考文件或脚本。这张图说明预期读取路线，不是实际执行轨迹，也不是权限控制。 官方 skill 说明 ↗ 外部参考 Design Council · 双钻模型 问题发现与不同解决方向的探索。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/ux-rethinking.html","anchor":"start","page":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"title":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"text":{"en":"Draft 0.1 UX Rethinking Reimagine a working feature around the user’s outcome. Preserve real capability and quality while reducing the work users must do.","zh":"初稿 0.1 UX 重构 围绕用户结果，重新构想已有功能。 保留真实能力与质量，减少用户必须承担的工作。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/ux-rethinking.html","anchor":"baseline","page":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"title":{"en":"Establish the real baseline","zh":"建立真实基线"},"text":{"en":"Establish the real baseline Read the implemented capability before judging the experience. Product documents describe intent; code, contracts, fixtures, and observed behavior establish different parts of the current state. Capability evidence Read the real paths and limits. User job Define the outcome and decisions. Responsibility Move resolvable work into the system. Target experience Rebuild objects, flow, and content. Source What it establishes Boundary Documents Intended behavior, scope, and decisions. Check approval and freshness; intent does not establish execution. Code and contracts Implemented paths, states, validations, and dependencies. Verify registration, reachability, and real composition. Fixtures and runtime Fixtures illustrate states; observed runs show behavior for a scenario. Label demo-only, partial, live-verified, and unknown capability. Baseline inspection checklist Record branch, commit, worktree, dirty files, routes, components, service calls, and provider boundaries. Walk the entry-to-result path, including permission, loading, empty, stale, partial, and returning states. Identify actions that really execute and claims that only exist in UI or fixtures.","zh":"建立真实基线 判断体验前，先理解已经实现的能力。产品文档说明意图；代码、契约、fixture 与实际运行分别提供不同层面的现状证据。 能力证据 读取真实路径与限制。 用户任务 定义结果与必要决定。 责任 让系统承担能解决的工作。 目标体验 重建对象、流程与内容。 来源 说明什么 边界 产品文档 预期行为、范围与决定。 核对批准与时效；意图不能证明已经执行。 代码与契约 已实现路径、状态、校验与依赖。 核对注册、可达性与真实组合路径。 Fixture 与运行 Fixture 展示示意状态；实际运行说明特定场景行为。 标明演示、部分实现、运行验证与未知能力。 基线检查项 记录分支、提交、工作区、未提交改动、路由、组件、服务调用与供应商边界。 走完入口到结果的路径，覆盖权限、加载、空、过期、部分完成与返回状态。 区分实际执行的动作与只存在于 UI 或 fixture 的能力声明。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/ux-rethinking.html","anchor":"friction","page":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"title":{"en":"Diagnose friction and responsibility","zh":"诊断阻力与责任"},"text":{"en":"Diagnose friction and responsibility Look for work that the interface asks users to do because the implementation has not resolved it. Keep human decisions when their consequences require judgment or authority. Friction Question Potential response Comprehension Can people tell what matters and what to do next? Organize around the task and primary decision. Input and choice Are users repeating known information or selecting internal mechanisms? Resolve trusted context and safe defaults; expose consequential choices. Trust and execution Are facts, advice, authority, and actual results distinguishable? Show source, readiness, action consequences, and verified state. Recovery Can people resume after partial success, timeout, or interruption? Preserve progress, reconcile state, and make safe next actions clear. Quality protection For every removed input or step, explain how trusted context, validated defaults, server logic, or an explicit gap replaces it. Verify that reduced effort preserves the required result.","zh":"诊断阻力与责任 检查界面是否因为实现尚未解决问题，而把工作推给用户；涉及重要后果、判断或权限的决定则保留给人。 阻力 检查问题 可能的改法 理解 用户是否知道什么重要、下一步做什么？ 围绕任务与主要决定组织信息。 输入与选择 是否重复输入已知信息，或选择内部技术机制？ 解析可靠上下文与安全默认值，展示会影响结果的选择。 信任与执行 事实、建议、权限和真实结果是否清楚区分？ 呈现来源、就绪条件、操作后果与已验证状态。 恢复 部分成功、超时或中断后能否继续？ 保留进度、核对状态，明确安全的下一步。 保护输出质量 每移除一项输入或步骤，都说明如何由可靠上下文、已验证默认值、服务端逻辑或明确缺口替代。验证投入降低后，所需结果仍然成立。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/ux-rethinking.html","anchor":"directions","page":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"title":{"en":"Choose the depth of change","zh":"选择重构深度"},"text":{"en":"Choose the depth of change Compare three levels of intervention against product maturity and the cost of keeping the current model. Recommend one direction with evidence. Direction What changes Best fit Conservative integration Correct major friction, truth, and authority issues within a mostly stable structure. The mental model works and specific defects dominate. Structural rethink Rework objects, information architecture, state, and primary flow. Useful capabilities are trapped in fragmented or implementation-led workflows. User-first reimagination Rebuild the experience from the user job and a new responsibility model. The existing product model creates unnecessary work or wrong expectations. Compare variations using the same scenario Use the same user, data, edge state, quality bar, and authority boundary. Compare time to understand, input burden, decision count, trust, recovery, migration cost, and risks. Draw side-by-side mockups only when a genuine structural choice remains.","zh":"选择重构深度 结合产品成熟度和保留当前模型的代价，比较三种改动深度，并以证据推荐方向。 方向 改变什么 适合情况 保守整合 在基本稳定的结构内修正严重阻力、真实性与权限问题。 心智模型基本有效，主要问题集中在局部。 结构重构 重做对象、信息架构、状态与主流程。 能力有用，但受困于割裂或工程导向的流程。 用户视角重新构想 从用户任务与新的责任模型重新构建体验。 现有产品模型持续制造额外工作或错误预期。 用同一场景比较不同方案 采用相同用户、数据、边缘状态、质量标准与权限边界。比较理解时间、输入负担、决定数量、信任、恢复、迁移成本与风险。仍有真正结构选择时，再制作并排 mockup。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/ux-rethinking.html","anchor":"information","page":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"title":{"en":"Give every information item a job","zh":"让每项信息服务一个用途"},"text":{"en":"Give every information item a job Retain the information needed for a good decision, express it at the right moment, and account for what replaces anything removed. Disposition Use it when Check Keep It directly supports the current task or decision. Meaning, source, and default visibility. Rewrite The information matters but its language or framing obscures its use. Outcome-led copy, correct units, and uncertainty. Progressive disclosure Experts or exceptional cases need detail. Keep decision-critical facts visible; make detail discoverable. Move It belongs to another object, stage, role, or destination. A clear destination and retrieval path. Remove It is redundant, unsupported, unactionable, or internal-only. Dependent contracts and the replacement for any useful function. Add Trust, readiness, decision quality, or recovery lacks necessary information. Owner, source, state, and ongoing maintenance. Illustrative text flow · review a suggested reply Moment User sees / decides System resolves / verifies Prepare The request, a proposed reply, and any material missing context. Gather permitted facts and produce a versioned draft. Review Key sources and consequences; edit or approve. Validate required rules and check readiness. Act / recover Verified delivery state, or a clear pending/recovery state. Execute only with authority; read back result and reconcile timeout before retry.","zh":"让每项信息服务一个用途 保留好决策所需的信息，在正确时机表达，并交代被移除内容由什么替代。 处理方式 适用条件 检查什么 Keep · 保留 直接支持当前任务或决定。 含义、来源与默认可见性。 Rewrite · 改写 信息有用，但语言或表达方式遮蔽了用途。 结果导向文案、正确单位与不确定性。 Progressive disclosure · 渐进展示 专家或特殊情况需要详情。 决策关键信息保持可见，详情入口容易发现。 Move · 移动 更适合另一个对象、阶段、角色或位置。 明确去向与找回路径。 Remove · 移除 重复、无依据、无法行动，或只服务内部实现。 依赖契约，以及仍有用的功能由什么替代。 Add · 补充 信任、就绪、决定质量或恢复缺少必要信息。 负责人、来源、状态与后续维护。 示意文字 flow · 审阅建议回复 时机 用户看到与决定 系统解决与验证 准备 请求、建议回复与重要上下文缺口。 获取允许使用的事实，生成带版本草稿。 审阅 关键来源与后果，选择修改或批准。 验证必要规则与就绪条件。 行动或恢复 已验证发送状态，或清晰的待确认与恢复状态。 获得授权才执行；回读结果，超时后先核对再重试。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/ux-rethinking.html","anchor":"migration","page":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"title":{"en":"Validate one structural slice","zh":"验证一条结构性切片"},"text":{"en":"Validate one structural slice Separate UX/content changes from frontend, backend, and data-contract changes. Implement only the approved slice, then compare the real experience with the baseline. Friction and output quality Check comprehension, inputs, decisions, recovery effort, and whether the result remains accurate and useful. Capability truth and safety Verify actual responses, permissions, readiness, idempotency, partial outcomes, and recovery. Migration contract Proposal ID, selected direction, user outcome, scope, and preserved behavior. Affected UI/content, frontend, backend/API, data sources, and migration dependencies. Acceptance evidence, test/eval plan, rollout boundary, and rollback strategy. Prioritize misleading claims and broken authority, then a complete path, then broader visual and advanced capability work.","zh":"验证一条结构性切片 区分 UX 与内容、前端、后端和数据契约改动。只实现已批准切片，再把真实体验与基线比较。 用户阻力与输出质量 检查理解、输入、决定和恢复投入，以及结果是否仍然准确、有用。 能力真实性与执行安全 验证真实响应、权限、就绪、幂等、部分结果与恢复。 迁移契约 提案编号、选定方向、用户结果、范围与保持不变的行为。 受影响的 UI 与内容、前端、后端与 API、数据源和迁移依赖。 验收证据、测试与 eval 计划、上线边界与回滚策略。 先处理误导声明与权限问题，再验证完整路径，之后扩展视觉系统与高级能力。"}},{"path":"product-ux-rethinking/ux-rethinking.html","anchor":"files","page":{"en":"UX Rethinking","zh":"UX 重构"},"title":{"en":"Files and references","zh":"文件结构与参考"},"text":{"en":"Files and references File relationships for this module. Use the workflow sections above for the practical steps. Internal files View this folder on GitHub ↗ Entry README.md Shared file dependencies Task and authority ../_shared/task-contract.md Shared restructuring method ( EN / 简中 ) 00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md Workflow branches Rethink an existing MVP ( EN / 简中 ) 01-existing-mvp-ux-reimagination.en.md Plan a new feature ( EN / 简中 ) 02-new-feature-product-planning.en.md Supporting files · read when needed Product research ../product-research/README.md For missing user or task evidence. AI system audit ../ai-product-system-audit/README.md For material wiring, harness or contract uncertainty. Testing and eval ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md For concrete quality, reliability or comparative measurement. Delivery and learning ../delivery-learning/README.md For an approved migration slice. Context update discipline ../context-update-discipline/README.md When feedback changes the current scope or intent. Mermaid file map ↗ How the agent reads these files This page starts with an existing MVP. If the product model itself is unsettled, the README can route to framing first; it does not require both routes every time. This package currently starts from the README you give the agent. An installed skill is discovered through its name and description, then its SKILL.md is loaded; references and scripts support the selected task. These maps describe intended reading routes, not a live execution trace or an access-control mechanism. Official skill documentation ↗ External references No separate external method source is recorded for this module; its core method is the internal restructuring workflow.","zh":"文件结构与参考 本模块的文件关系。具体做法见上方工作流内容。 内部文件 在 GitHub 查看本模块文件夹 ↗ 入口 README.md 共用文件 任务与操作边界 ../_shared/task-contract.md 通用重构方法 ( EN / 简中 ) 00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md 工作流分支 重新构想已有 MVP ( EN / 简中 ) 01-existing-mvp-ux-reimagination.en.md 规划新功能 ( EN / 简中 ) 02-new-feature-product-planning.en.md 支持文件 · 按需读取 产品研究 ../product-research/README.md 缺少用户或任务证据时读取。 AI 系统审查 ../ai-product-system-audit/README.md 接入、harness 或契约存在关键不确定性时读取。 测试与评估 ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md 需要具体质量、可靠性或对照衡量方案时读取。 交付与复盘 ../delivery-learning/README.md 进入已批准的迁移切片时读取。 上下文更新规范 ../context-update-discipline/README.md 反馈改变当前范围或意图时读取。 查看 Mermaid 文件图 ↗ Agent 如何读取这些文件 本页以已有 MVP 为起点。产品模型本身尚未确定时，README 可先引导产品定义；并非每次都要跑两条路线。 当前 package 从你交给 Agent 的 README 开始。已安装的 skill 会先通过名称和描述被发现，再读取 SKILL.md，并按任务使用参考文件或脚本。这张图说明预期读取路线，不是实际执行轨迹，也不是权限控制。 官方 skill 说明 ↗ 外部参考 此模块目前未单独记录外部方法来源；核心方法来自内部重构工作流。"}},{"path":"testing-evaluation-system/testing-evaluation-system.html","anchor":"start","page":{"en":"Testing & Evaluation System","zh":"测试与评估系统"},"title":{"en":"Testing & Evaluation System","zh":"测试与评估系统"},"text":{"en":"From evidence to a decision Testing & Evaluation System Find out whether a feature works, how well it performs, and what to improve next. Every feature needs an evidence strategy. Decide what you need to know, how to check it, and what result would change your next action. Tests, evals, comparisons, and real-use signals can work together.","zh":"从证据到决策 测试与评估系统 判断功能是否正常、效果够不够好，以及下一步该改进什么。 每个功能都需要一套证据策略。 先明确需要知道什么、如何验证，以及什么结果会改变下一步行动。测试、eval、方案比较与真实使用信号可以配合使用。"}},{"path":"testing-evaluation-system/testing-evaluation-system.html","anchor":"choose","page":{"en":"Testing & Evaluation System","zh":"测试与评估系统"},"title":{"en":"Choose a combination around the decision","zh":"围绕当前决策，选择验证组合"},"text":{"en":"Choose evidence Choose a combination around the decision The scope can be a function, a stage, a task, or an entire feature. Select measurements that resolve the uncertainty behind your next action. 1 · Measure Tests Check behavior with precise assertions—for example, saved data matches the submitted values. Evals Measure output quality and task performance—for example, whether generated content is accurate, relevant, and usable. 2 · Apply measurements Benchmark Compare candidates with shared measures → choose which version, model, or workflow to adopt. Production validation Check real-use quality and reliability → expand rollout, fix issues, or roll back. Controlled experiment Estimate the effect caused by a change → adopt, revise, or stop it. 3 · Make it repeatable Shared definitions, cases, execution, and records Preserve what ran and how it was judged so the next version can be compared fairly. Use direct assertions for checkable behavior; combine metrics and judgment to assess task performance. Tests can also serve as graders inside an eval, alongside quality, cost, and latency measures. When to use it How to organize it Methods and materials Decision supported Verify directly checkable behavior Tests Assert expected values, states, permissions, or invariants, from individual steps to the full path. For example, an unauthorized save must be rejected. Unit · Contract · Integration · E2E; add robustness, failure injection, or load checks as needed. Pass/fail, first failing boundary, and whether release must stop. Assess output or task performance Evals Define quality dimensions and operating metrics; combine code, model, and human graders. Offline / online eval · golden set · rubric · code grader · model judge · human review. Strengths, weak scenarios, uncertainty, and the next quality improvement. Choose a version, model, or workflow Benchmark Apply comparable tests, evals, and operating metrics to each candidate. Relevant baseline · shared cases or golden set · pairwise comparison · repeated runs. Whether the gain justifies cost and complexity, with protected capabilities checked for regression. Validate real-use performance Production validation Combine online checks, online evals, monitoring, and usage signals. Trace review · drift monitoring · shadow / canary · rollback gates. Expand rollout, fix, or roll back; capture new cases for offline checks. Estimate the effect of a change Controlled experiments Predefine assignment, exposure, metrics, and analysis when traffic and risk permit. A/B · A/A infrastructure checks where needed · guardrail metrics. Adopt, iterate, or stop; explain which users and conditions the estimate applies to. Compose around the evidence gap. A prompt revision may need only offline eval; a permission change may mainly need tests; an AI workflow may combine contract tests, output eval, and production validation. A shared harness should preserve the meaning of rule failures, weak quality, invalid runs, and insufficient evidence. Method reference · golden set, robustness, A/B, and rollout patterns These tools can support several approaches above. Choose one when it closes a specific evidence gap. Name Role in the system When to add it Golden set · Reference cases Case asset for tests, evals, and benchmarks. Curated cases carry reviewed reference answers or expected judgments. Use for stable version comparisons, regression checks, or grader calibration. Version the set and keep independent held-out cases. Robustness checks Coverage method: vary inputs, context, or operating conditions; measure both rule compliance and changes in quality. Use when missing information, noise, distribution shifts, or dependency failures can affect performance. Load / stress tests Operational method: measure capacity, latency, degradation, and recovery under traffic or resource pressure. Use to establish supported scale and what happens when capacity is exceeded. Red-team / blue-team exercises Adversarial assurance: challenge safety and permission boundaries, then validate defenses and response. Use for abuse paths, unauthorized actions, and other high-risk behavior. Record findings as repeatable cases where possible. A/B and A/A Experiment designs: A/B compares different treatments; A/A uses identical treatments to check assignment and measurement. Use A/B for causal effect estimates; use A/A when validating new or materially changed experiment infrastructure. Shadow and canary Release patterns: shadow runs a candidate alongside live traffic without applying its outputs; canary exposes a small controlled share to the new version. Use for real-environment evidence with controlled rollout risk. Isolate shadow side effects; define monitoring and rollback gates for canaries. Combine rule checks, quality judgments and repeated runs Tests and evals can use the same cases. Build the combination by choosing how to judge each requirement, then deciding whether repeated runs are needed to understand variability. Check directly verifiable rules. Use deterministic checks for required fields, value limits or permission rules. With a fixed rule, the same recorded input and output produce the same verdict. Judge contextual quality. Define clear criteria for qualities such as relevance and usefulness, then use qualified human review or a validated model judge to assess them. Measure variation when it matters. When the same task produces varying results, repeat it as needed and apply the selected checks to each result. Use success rates or score distributions, with uncertainty, to assess how reliably the system meets the criteria.","zh":"选择验证方式 围绕当前决策，选择验证组合 验证范围可以是一段逻辑、一个处理环节、一次任务或整个功能。选择能解决当前不确定性、支持下一步行动的衡量方式。 1 · 核心衡量 测试 test 用精确断言检查行为，例如保存后读回的数据与提交值一致。 评估 eval 衡量输出质量与任务表现，例如生成内容是否准确、切题，并满足实际使用需要。 2 · 组织证据 方案比较 benchmark 用共同指标比较候选方案 → 决定采用哪个版本、模型或工作流。 生产环境验证 production validation 检查真实使用中的质量与可靠性 → 决定扩大上线、修复或回滚。 受控实验 controlled experiment 估计改动本身带来的效果 → 决定采用、调整或停止。 3 · 系统基础 统一定义、案例、执行与记录 保存运行了什么、如何判断，才能在下一次改版时公平比较。 可直接判定的行为用断言检查；任务表现则结合指标与质量判断。Tests 也可以作为 eval 中的评分依据，与质量、成本和延迟指标一起使用。 什么时候用 如何组织验证 常用方法与材料 支持什么决定 检查可直接断言的行为与约束 测试 test 从单步到完整路径，检查预期值、状态、权限或必须保持的规则。例如，无权限的保存请求应被拒绝。 Unit · Contract · Integration · E2E；按需加入鲁棒性、故障注入或负载检查。 是否满足要求、最早失败的边界，以及是否阻止发布。 衡量输出或任务表现 评估 eval 定义质量维度与运行指标，组合代码、模型和人工评分。 Offline / online eval · golden set · rubric · code grader · model judge · 人工审核。 哪些能力足够好、哪些场景薄弱，以及下一轮改进重点。 选择版本、模型或工作流 方案比较 benchmark 让候选方案接受可比较的 tests、eval 和运行指标衡量。 相关 baseline · 共享案例或 golden set · 成对比较 · 重复运行。 改善是否值得成本与复杂度，以及关键能力是否退步。 确认真实使用中的表现 生产环境验证 production validation 结合线上检查、online eval、监控与使用信号。 Trace 抽查 · 漂移监测 · shadow / canary · 回滚门槛。 扩大上线、修复或回滚；把真实案例补入离线验证。 判断改动带来的产品效果 受控实验 controlled experiment 在流量与风险允许时，预先确定分组、曝光、指标和分析计划。 A/B · 按需用 A/A 检查实验链路 · guardrail 保护指标。 采用、迭代或停止，并明确效果估计适用的用户与条件。 根据证据缺口组合。 一次 prompt 优化可能只需要离线 eval；权限修改可能主要需要 tests；AI 工作流则可能组合契约测试、输出 eval 和线上验证。共用执行与报告体系时，分别保留规则失败、质量不足、运行无效和证据不足的含义。 方法速查 · Golden set、鲁棒性、A/B 与发布方式 这些方法与材料可以用于上表中的多种验证方式。根据需要补齐的证据选择。 名称 在系统中的作用 什么时候加入 精选参考案例集 golden set 案例资产：为 tests、eval 和 benchmark 提供经过审核的参考案例与预期判断。 需要稳定比较版本、检查回归或校准评分者时使用。管理集合版本，并保留独立留出案例。 鲁棒性检查 robustness 覆盖方法：改变输入、上下文或运行条件，同时观察规则是否成立、质量如何变化。 产品会遇到缺失信息、噪声、分布变化或依赖故障时加入。 负载与压力测试 load / stress test 运行性能方法：衡量流量或资源压力下的容量、延迟、降级与恢复。 需要判断可承受的规模，以及超出容量后如何表现时使用。 Red-team / blue-team · 红蓝队演练 对抗性验证：主动挑战安全与权限边界，再验证防御和响应。 需要发现滥用路径、越权执行等高风险行为时使用。把可复现的发现转成后续案例。 A/B 与 A/A 实验设计：A/B 比较不同方案；A/A 用相同方案检查分组和衡量链路。 A/B 用于效果归因；实验基础设施新建或发生重要变化时，可用 A/A 检查异常。 Shadow 与 canary 发布方式：Shadow 在真实流量旁运行候选版本但不执行其输出；Canary 让受控的小部分流量实际使用新版本。 需要控制上线风险并获取真实环境证据时使用。隔离影子运行的副作用，为 canary 设置监控与回滚门槛。 如何组合规则检查、质量判断与重复运行 测试 test 与评估 eval 可以共用一批案例。组合时，先选择每项要求的判定方式，再根据结果波动决定是否需要重复运行： 检查能直接判定的规则。 必需字段、数值范围或权限规则可用确定性检查 deterministic checks。在规则固定时，对同一份输入与输出记录会得到相同判定。 判断需要结合语境的质量。 对相关性、实用性等质量明确评分标准，再由具备相应知识的人或经过验证的模型判定。 在波动影响决策时重复运行。 同一任务的结果有波动时，按需要重复运行，每次都使用选定的判定方式。结合成功率或得分分布及其不确定性，判断系统达到标准的稳定程度。"}},{"path":"testing-evaluation-system/testing-evaluation-system.html","anchor":"design","page":{"en":"Testing & Evaluation System","zh":"测试与评估系统"},"title":{"en":"Design the verification","zh":"设计验证"},"text":{"en":"Design the verification Turn the selected approach into cases, observable criteria and an interpretation rule. Define the common foundation, then open only the method designs needed for this decision. Cases, criteria and judgment Define the inputs and conditions, the expected behavior, and how each result will be judged. Together, these make the selected verification approach executable. Scenario axes Which variations should cases cover? The same feature may behave differently across users, inputs, permissions, and operating conditions. Use axes to choose cases systematically. Criteria What counts as good? Define invariants, quality dimensions, scoring anchors, thresholds, operating limits, and capabilities to protect. Graders How will results be judged? Use code for exact rules and validated model or human judgment for contextual quality. Keep evidence and uncertainty with the score. Coverage dimensions User and domain Goal and lifecycle Input variability Contextual complexity Personalization and customization Risk and authority Tool or provider state Scale and load Scenario axes · selection questions and examples Select the axes that materially change performance or risk. Input completeness and context consistency are separate axes: a complete brief can still contain conflicting facts. Coverage dimension What to consider Examples User and domain Do requirements change across users or domains? New and experienced users; different professional domains. Goal and lifecycle What is the task, and where is the user in it? First creation, editing existing content, retry, or recovery. Input variability Which supported representations or information gaps could change the result? Equivalent facts in supported formats or media; missing fields; damaged or unsupported input. Contextual complexity Which intents and facts remain active across evidence, corrections and history? Competing intents, ambiguous tool fields, stale evidence, or a corrected fact in a long conversation. Risk and authority What are the consequences of error, and what actions are allowed? Read-only advice, editing access, or approval required before execution. Tool or provider state How does the feature behave when dependencies change? Normal, timeout, rate limit, or partial results. Scale and load Does input size or workload change performance? Large inputs, concurrent requests, or batch tasks. Personalization and customization What may adapt, and which requirements remain protected? A requested writing style or output shape; conflicting instructions; saved preference changes only if persistence exists. Prioritize frequent tasks, high-risk cases, and known failures. Add important combinations, such as sparse input plus authority to execute. Choose combinations by risk rather than enumerating every permutation. For selected variations, specify the original conditions, what changes, expected behavior and how to observe it. Include normal cases; add combinations only when they reflect a real risk. Check whether behavior should stay stable, adapt, ask for clarification or follow a safe fallback. A formatting option does not imply memory, tool or multi-agent coverage. Case-design reference → Dataset partitions · development, regression, calibration, and held-out Separate cases by their purpose and record any overlap. Repeatedly tuning against the final assessment cases makes the result less informative about unseen work. Partition Use Development set Tune the implementation, prompts, and rubric. Regression set Check that known capabilities and previous fixes still hold. Calibration set Check grader reliability against reviewed judgments. Held-out set Assess performance on cases not used during tuning. Choose and combine evaluators Choose what to assess and how to judge it separately. Code, people and models can return labels or numbers: a human can rate usefulness from 1–5, and a model can return pass/fail. Quantitative results do not by themselves establish deterministic or valid judgment. Mechanism Use it for Check its limits Code checks and metrics Rule and state assertions; defined quantities such as error rate, latency and cost Check the oracle, formula, units and denominator; runtime measurements vary, and structural validity does not establish quality Human eval Domain usefulness, ambiguous cases and calibration labels Relevant expertise, evidence, anchors and how disagreements are resolved LLM-as-a-judge Repeated contextual assessments against a clear rubric Agreement with qualified human review, order/length bias and invalid judge responses Combine mechanisms for distinct responsibilities: code checks output structure, then a person or validated judge checks meaning and usefulness. Keep mandatory failures separate from quality scores; unresolved grading is not a product pass or fail. Grader validity · check scoring before using it for decisions A grader can reward a fluent but incorrect answer. Check it on strong, weak, borderline, and serious-failure cases before using its scores for release decisions. Provide the source facts and context needed to judge each criterion. Define concrete scoring anchors; keep reasons tied to observable evidence. Compare with qualified human ratings using defined agreement or error measures. Inspect missed serious failures and false alarms; use independent confirmation when needed after tuning. Blind candidate identity where practical to reduce preference bias. Version the model, instructions, rubric, context, and parser. Revalidate after material changes and define how disputes are adjudicated. Eval matrix · connect cases to criteria Use a matrix to connect cases, applicable criteria and graders. First define each case's expected behavior: produce, clarify, decline or recover. A correct decline may pass without generated content to score. Keep expectations, measured results and unmeasured cells distinct. Case Check Judgment A generated recommendation Required fields are present Code assertion → pass / fail The same recommendation Advice is supported and usable Anchored human or validated model judgment For more detailed grader selection and calibration, load only the relevant reference. Grader design → Method designs · open what you need Test Check specified behavior at the relevant boundary. Question Does the required behavior hold, including consequential failure paths? Design Choose the function, contract, service or end-to-end boundary. Set input and initial state, trigger the action, then assert the expected return, saved state or side effect. Use isolated fixtures for risky operations. Read the result Inspect failed assertions and the first divergence. Distinguish product defects from broken fixtures or environments; use passing checks only for the boundary they exercise. Avoid misreading A helper test or valid intermediate object does not establish consumer read-back. Exact text equality is unsuitable when several outputs are valid. Detailed workflow reference → Eval Assess task performance against explicit criteria. Question How well does the system meet the intended task and quality requirements? Design Select representative cases and material edge cases. Define anchors and acceptance before the run; choose code, human or validated model grading by criterion. Repeat stochastic runs when the decision needs an estimate of variation. Read the result Report applicable criterion results, hard failures, weak segments and uncertainty. Keep missing evidence visible and use held-out cases for claims about unseen work. Avoid misreading A high average can hide a critical failure. A numerical judge score is not automatically objective, and an offline score does not establish business impact. Detailed workflow reference → Benchmark Choose the comparison that answers the decision. Question Is a version better, is the product worth using, or does one component contribute? Design Research credible alternatives and their current capabilities before choosing a baseline. Compare a change with the current version, product value with a realistic alternative such as a manual process or general-purpose AI, and component contribution with a controlled ablation. Use matched tasks and shared criteria; document information access, versions, settings and user effort. Read the result Compare quality, protected capabilities, cost and user effort against pre-agreed meaningful differences. Tie conclusions to what differs between arms: checking an unchanged component for regression does not establish its superiority. Report uncertainty before choosing whether to adopt, iterate or retain the baseline. Avoid misreading A weak comparator inflates value. Equal-information and natural-use comparisons answer different questions; a whole-product comparison cannot isolate one component. Relative preference alone does not prove either option is acceptable. Detailed workflow reference → Production validation Check whether real use matches the supported claims. Question Does quality and reliability hold for real users, inputs and dependencies? Design Choose sampled online eval, monitoring or an authorized shadow/canary rollout for the uncertainty. Define segments, observation window, quality criteria, alerts and rollback rules; isolate shadow side effects and protect user data. Read the result Compare errors, latency and sampled task quality with agreed limits. Inspect weak segments and unexpected failures; decide to continue, repair or roll back, and turn verified failures into reusable cases. Avoid misreading A quiet dashboard can mean missing instrumentation. A small rollout does not establish all-user readiness, and metric movement alone does not prove causality. Detailed workflow reference → Controlled experiment Estimate whether a change caused an outcome. Question Did the intervention improve an outcome, rather than merely coincide with it? Design Define hypothesis, treatment, assignment unit, exposure and primary/guardrail metrics. Randomize where feasible; plan sample size, duration and stopping/analysis rules, checking interference and measurement quality. Use the analytics workflow for detailed design. Read the result Report effect size and uncertainty, metric guardrails, valid exposure and which population the estimate applies to. Assess practical value as well as statistical evidence. Avoid misreading Before/after movement or a canary is not automatically a randomized experiment. Repeated peeking or changing metrics after seeing results can invalidate the conclusion. Detailed workflow reference →","zh":"设计验证 把选定方式转成案例、可观察标准和结果解释规则。先确定共用基础，再按本轮决策展开需要的方法。 案例、标准与判定 明确检查所用的输入与条件、预期行为，以及每项结果如何判定，让选定的验证方式能够实际执行。 场景维度 覆盖哪些变化？ 同一个功能在不同用户、输入、权限或运行条件下可能表现不同。用场景维度系统地选择案例，发现正常输入之外的问题。 评估标准 什么算好？ 定义必须成立的规则、质量维度、评分锚点、阈值、运行限制，以及需要保护的已有能力。 判定方式 如何判断结果？ 明确规则交给代码判断；语义与实用性可由经过验证的模型或人判断。分数需要带上证据与不确定性。 覆盖维度 用户与业务领域 目标与生命周期阶段 输入变化 input variability 上下文复杂度 contextual complexity 个性化与定制 风险与权限 工具或供应商状态 规模与负载 场景维度 · 选择问题与具体例子 选择会明显影响表现或风险的维度。输入完整程度与上下文一致性是两个维度：资料齐全，也可能存在事实冲突。 覆盖维度 要考虑什么 示例 用户与业务领域 不同用户或领域是否有不同要求？ 新手与熟练用户；不同专业领域。 目标与生命周期阶段 用户正在完成什么任务，处于哪个阶段？ 首次创建、修改已有内容、重试或恢复失败任务。 输入变化 input variability 语言、结构、模态或资料缺失会怎样影响结果？ 相同事实的不同格式或模态；缺少字段；损坏或不支持的输入。 上下文复杂度 contextual complexity 多意图、证据冲突和历史更正中，哪些要求与事实仍然有效？ 多项请求、含糊的工具字段、过期来源、长对话中的事实更正。 风险与权限 出错有什么后果，系统被允许做什么？ 只读建议、可修改、需人工批准后执行。 工具或供应商状态 外部依赖出现变化时会怎样？ 正常、超时、限流、部分结果缺失。 规模与负载 输入大小或任务负载是否改变表现？ 大体积输入、并发请求、批量任务。 个性化与定制 personalization and customization 哪些内容允许随偏好改变，哪些要求必须保持？ 指定语气或输出格式；冲突指令；仅在支持保存偏好时检查偏好更新。 优先覆盖高频场景、高风险场景和已知失败，再补充关键组合，例如“信息不足＋允许外部执行”。按风险选择组合，无须穷举所有排列。 每项选中的变化都写清：原始条件、改变什么、预期行为、如何观察。保留正常案例，只为真实风险增加组合。 判断结果应保持稳定、按需适配、澄清还是安全降级。仅支持格式定制的功能，不需要因此增加记忆、工具或多 Agent 测试。 查看边界案例设计 → 数据集分区 · 开发、回归、校准与留出 按用途管理案例，并记录集合之间的重叠。反复用最终评估案例调试，会削弱结果对新任务表现的说明力。 分区 用途 开发集 用于调试实现、prompt 与评分标准。 回归集 检查已有能力与已修复问题是否退步。 校准集 对照审核过的判断，检查评分方式是否可靠。 留出集 检验在未用于调试的案例上是否仍然有效。 选择与组合判定方式 evaluators 分别确定评什么，以及如何判断。代码、人工和模型都可以返回标签或数字：人工可以给实用性打 1–5 分，模型也可以判通过／失败。量化结果 quantitative 本身不代表判定是确定性的 deterministic，或分数有效。 判定方式 适合判断什么 需要核实什么 代码检查与指标 code-based 规则与状态断言；错误率、延迟、成本等明确量值 核实参考答案、公式、单位和分母；运行测量会波动，结构通过不代表内容优质 人工评估 human eval 专业实用性、难判断案例与校准标签 审核能力、依据、评分锚点与分歧处理方式 模型判定 LLM-as-a-judge 依据明确标准反复判断语义与质量 与合格人工审核的一致性、顺序／长度偏好、评分器异常 按职责组合：代码检查输出结构，人工或经过验证的模型检查语义与实用性。必要条件失败与质量分数分开；评分未完成或无效，不等于产品通过或失败。 评分可靠性 · 用分数做决定前要检查什么 评分者可能给流畅但错误的答案打高分。先用优秀、较差、临界和严重失败案例检查评分表现，再用分数支持发布决定。 提供判断每项标准所需的原始事实与上下文。 定义具体评分锚点，并让评分理由对应可观察的证据。 用定义清楚的一致性或误差指标，与合格人工评分比较。检查漏掉的严重失败与误报；调优后按结论需要补充独立确认。 条件允许时隐藏候选方案身份，减少偏好带来的影响。 记录模型、指令、rubric、上下文与解析器版本；重要变更后重新验证，并明确评分争议如何裁定。 评估矩阵 eval matrix · 把案例与标准对应起来 用矩阵连接案例、适用标准与评分方式。先确定每个案例应生成、追问、拒绝还是恢复：正确拒绝可以通过行为检查，但没有生成内容可评分。预期、实测结果与尚未测量的部分分别记录。 案例 检查 判定方式 一条生成建议 必需字段齐全 代码断言 → 通过／失败 同一条生成建议 建议有依据且可用 带评分锚点的人工判断或已验证模型判断 需要更详细的评分方式选择与校准时，按需读取参考文件。 判定方式设计 → 方法设计 · 按需展开 测试 test 在相关边界检查明确要求。 要回答的问题 要求的行为是否成立，包括重要失败路径？ 具体怎么设计 选择函数、契约、服务或端到端边界。设置输入与初始状态，触发操作，再断言返回值、保存状态或副作用。高风险操作使用隔离案例。 看什么结果 查看失败断言与最早偏离点，区分产品缺陷和案例／环境异常；通过结果只支持实际检查过的边界。 常见误判 辅助函数通过或中间对象合法，不代表下游实际读回正确；存在多种有效输出时不宜要求文本完全相同。 查看详细工作流 → 评估 eval 按明确标准判断任务表现。 要回答的问题 系统满足任务与质量要求的程度如何？ 具体怎么设计 选择代表案例与重要边界案例。运行前定义评分锚点和验收条件，按标准选择代码、人工或已验证模型判定；决策需要了解波动时，再安排重复运行。 看什么结果 报告适用标准的结果、硬性失败、薄弱场景和不确定性。保留缺失证据，判断新任务泛化能力时使用留出案例。 常见误判 高均分可能掩盖关键失败。模型给出数字不代表客观，离线分数也不能直接证明业务效果。 查看详细工作流 → 方案比较 benchmark 按决策选择真正有用的对照。 要回答的问题 新版本是否更好、产品是否值得用，或某个组件是否有贡献？ 具体怎么设计 先了解用户实际可选的做法及其当前能力，再确定基线 baseline。版本改动与当前版比；产品价值与人工流程、现有工具或通用 AI 等真实替代方案比；组件贡献用受控消融。使用可比较任务和统一标准，说明资料访问差异，记录版本、设置与用户投入。 看什么结果 按预先约定的有意义差异，比较质量、受保护能力、成本与用户投入。结论应对应两组实际改变的因素：检查未改变的组件是否退步，并不能证明它优于其他方案。结合不确定性决定采用、改进或保留基线。 常见误判 过弱的对照会夸大价值。相同资料与自然使用比较回答不同问题；整产品比较不能隔离组件贡献。相对更好也不代表达到可用标准。 查看详细工作流 → 生产环境验证 production validation 检查真实使用是否符合已支持的结论。 要回答的问题 面对真实用户、输入与依赖时，质量和可靠性是否仍然成立？ 具体怎么设计 按不确定性选择线上抽样评估、监控或获准的影子／小流量发布。定义用户群、观察窗口、质量标准、告警与回滚条件，隔离影子运行副作用并保护用户数据。 看什么结果 对照约定界限检查错误、延迟和抽样任务质量，关注薄弱群体与意外失败；决定继续、修复或回滚，把确认的失败转为案例。 常见误判 看板无告警也可能是埋点缺失。小流量正常不代表全量就绪，指标变化本身不证明因果。 查看详细工作流 → 受控实验 controlled experiment 估计某项改动是否造成结果变化。 要回答的问题 结果改善是否由这次改动造成，而不只是同时发生？ 具体怎么设计 定义假设、改动、分配单位、实际接触以及主指标与保护指标。可行时随机分配，规划样本量、时长及停止／分析规则，检查组间干扰与衡量质量。详细设计进入产品分析工作流。 看什么结果 报告效果大小与不确定性、保护指标、有效曝光和适用人群。同时判断实际价值与统计证据。 常见误判 前后变化或小流量发布不自动构成随机实验。反复查看结果后提前停止，或事后更换指标，都可能破坏结论有效性。 查看详细工作流 →"}},{"path":"testing-evaluation-system/testing-evaluation-system.html","anchor":"system","page":{"en":"Testing & Evaluation System","zh":"测试与评估系统"},"title":{"en":"Connect the parts into a repeatable loop","zh":"把各部分连成一个可重复的闭环"},"text":{"en":"How the system works Connect the parts into a repeatable loop An eval contract sets decision rules. Cases pass through execution and judgment; records preserve evidence for analysis, review and improvement. Several methods can share these responsibilities; a small project can use shared scripts and files. Define 1 · Eval contract Agree how evidence will support a decision. 2 · Scenario registry Keep coverage deliberate and reusable. Run 3 · Stage contracts Isolate selected boundaries when the decision requires it. 4 · Runner Execute the chosen cases under controlled conditions. Assess 5 · Graders Measure each criterion with a validated method. Record 6 · Run manifest Make results traceable and comparisons reproducible. Decide 7 · Analysis and decisions Turn evidence into prioritized action. Feed confirmed findings into the feature, cases, and graders, then run again. Implementation reference · contracts, runner, graders, and run records The harness connects cases, execution, graders, and records. Gates define whether the evidence is sufficient to proceed. Part Purpose What to specify 1 · Eval contract Agree how evidence will support a decision. Decision, evaluation unit, criteria, thresholds, hard limits, and actions for pass, fail, or insufficient evidence. 2 · Scenario registry Keep coverage deliberate and reusable. Stable case IDs and versions, coverage axes, rationale, risk, expected behavior, and dataset partitions. 3 · Stage contracts Isolate selected boundaries when the decision requires it. Input/output schemas, required fields, provenance, and failure states. Freeze versioned handoffs to isolate a stage from upstream changes. 4 · Runner Execute the chosen cases under controlled conditions. Deterministic, replay, benchmark, and approved live paths; explicit budgets, permissions, timeouts, and side-effect controls. 5 · Graders Measure each criterion with a validated method. Assertions, metrics, anchored rubrics, model judges, or human ratings; record evidence and validate scoring reliability. 6 · Run manifest Make results traceable and comparisons reproducible. Case, code, model, prompt, and grader versions; environment, context, artifacts, traces, failures, cost, and latency. 7 · Analysis and decisions Turn evidence into prioritized action. Agent diagnosis, uncertainty, protected regressions, focused human review, release gates, accountable decisions, and follow-up cases.","zh":"系统如何运作 把各部分连成一个可重复的闭环 评估约定 eval contract 确定决策规则；案例经过执行与判定，记录保留证据，再进入分析、审核和改进。同一套组件可以支持多种方法，简单项目可以共用脚本与文件。 定义 1 · 评估约定 Eval contract 提前约定证据如何支持决策。 2 · 场景库 Scenario registry 让覆盖范围有依据、案例可复用。 运行 3 · 环节契约 Stage contracts 按决策需要，隔离选定环节进行验证。 4 · 执行器 Runner 在可控条件下执行选定案例。 判断 5 · 评分方式 Graders 用已验证的方法衡量每项标准。 记录 6 · 运行清单 Run manifest 让结果可追溯、比较可复现。 行动 7 · 分析与决策 把证据转成有优先级的行动。 把确认的发现用于改进功能、案例和评分方式，再运行一次。 实施参考 · 契约、执行器、评分与运行记录 Harness 是把案例、执行、评分和记录连起来的运行框架；Gate 是判断证据是否足以支持继续行动的检查条件。 组成部分 用途 需要明确什么 1 · 评估约定 Eval contract 提前约定证据如何支持决策。 决策问题、评估单元、标准、阈值、硬性限制，以及通过、失败或证据不足时的行动。 2 · 场景库 Scenario registry 让覆盖范围有依据、案例可复用。 案例编号与版本、覆盖维度、选择理由、风险、预期行为和数据集分区。 3 · 环节契约 Stage contracts 按决策需要，隔离选定环节进行验证。 输入输出 schema、必需字段、来源与失败状态。保存固定版本的交接数据，避免上游变化干扰单环节比较。 4 · 执行器 Runner 在可控条件下执行选定案例。 确定性运行、回放、benchmark 与已批准的真实运行路径；明确预算、权限、超时和副作用控制。 5 · 评分方式 Graders 用已验证的方法衡量每项标准。 断言、指标、带评分锚点的 rubric、模型 judge 或人工评分；保留证据并验证评分可靠性。 6 · 运行清单 Run manifest 让结果可追溯、比较可复现。 案例、代码、模型、prompt 与 grader 版本；环境、上下文、产物、trace、失败记录、成本和延迟。 7 · 分析与决策 把证据转成有优先级的行动。 Agent 诊断、不确定性、受保护能力回退、重点人工审核、发布门槛、责任明确的决定与后续案例。"}},{"path":"testing-evaluation-system/testing-evaluation-system.html","anchor":"sequence","page":{"en":"Testing & Evaluation System","zh":"测试与评估系统"},"title":{"en":"From an evidence plan to ongoing use","zh":"从验证方案到持续使用"},"text":{"en":"Set up and use From an evidence plan to ongoing use Start where your system is today: design the checks, connect a runnable path, or analyze an existing run. Ask your agent to follow the matching workflow within the agreed permissions; production validation continues the same cycle after release. Define scope → Connect checks → Analyze and review → Learn from real use 1 1 · Define the decision and scope Choose the version or task scope and the evidence sufficient for this decision. Output: A bounded round: scope, checks, acceptance, stopping rules and deferred work. Design a plan → Review existing coverage → Actions and checkpoints Choose the scope from the decision and current product version. Reuse sound cases, runners and results; identify what needs adapting or adding. Keep inspected facts and design assumptions distinct. Select tests and evals for the actual risks. Link each check to its decision and prerequisites, so independent work can proceed while a specific dependency is resolved. Preserve required safety checks. For a comparison, establish a credible baseline: what users do today or which viable alternative they could use. Set acceptance and stopping rules before the run. Separate setup, automated workload and human review estimates; defer non-critical expansion with clear triggers. A budget stop preserves partial evidence, not a pass. 2 2 · Connect and verify one runnable path Reuse existing infrastructure; add only what the agreed plan needs. Output: A repeatable run with reliable grading and traceable records. Set up the agreed checks → Actions and checkpoints Prepare versioned cases and suitable partitions. Choose code, qualified human review or a validated model judge for each criterion. Record which criteria, tasks and decision uses the judge's validation covers. Connect selected stage contracts, runner, graders, saved artifacts, and replay. Start with a narrow path whose results you can inspect end to end. Agree permissions, budgets, external effects, and timeouts. Mark incomplete or broken measurement runs as invalid so they cannot be mistaken for product results. 3 3 · Run, analyze, and decide Let the agent run authorized checks and analyze the results first. Use its decision overview to focus human review on quality judgments, business trade-offs, and actions requiring approval. Output: A supported recommendation, focused review list, and next action. Run or analyze a round → Actions and checkpoints Run authorized checks or analyze saved results. Preserve original outputs, compare meaningful segments, and locate the first point where behavior diverges. Separate product failures from invalid measurements. Report uncertainty and protected regressions alongside quality, cost, latency, and user effort. For each human-review request, include the actual output, relevant input, criterion, agent assessment, and one specific question. Prioritize serious risks, borderline scores, grader disagreements, and unfamiliar failures; sample some passes to check for missed problems. Record the decision and its scope. Read the results for your decision Product · Connect results to user impact; choose the next product change. Engineering · Check reproducibility and locate the first failure; fix its cause within the agreed scope. Quality & operations · Review ambiguous or risky outputs against real workflow needs; decide whether they are ready for use. 4 4 · Validate real use and improve coverage After an approved rollout, check whether real-user tasks maintain the expected quality and reliability. Output: A rollout decision and reusable cases for the next version. Analyze the evidence → Analytics and experiments → Actions and checkpoints Monitor errors and latency; sample real outputs against the agreed quality criteria. Review weak user segments and tasks instead of relying only on an overall average. Use shadow or canary exposure where appropriate and authorized. Set alert and rollback conditions before exposure; isolate side effects in shadow runs. After review and de-identification, turn a real failure into an offline case with an expected result. Fix the issue, rerun relevant cases, and keep independent holdouts for future validation. To understand adoption, completion, or retention, use product analytics. To estimate whether a particular change caused an improvement, use an appropriately designed controlled experiment.","zh":"搭建与使用 从验证方案到持续使用 按当前状态选择起点：设计检查方案、接通运行路径，或分析已有结果。让 Agent 在约定权限内使用对应工作流；上线后的验证继续沿用这套循环。 明确范围 → 接通检查 → 分析与复核 → 真实使用反馈 1 1 · 明确决策与验证范围 明确本轮版本或任务范围，以及哪些证据足以支持这次决定。 产出： 本轮工作包：范围、检查、验收与停止条件，以及后续项。 设计验证方案 → 审查已有覆盖 → 具体做法与检查点 从当前决策和产品版本确定范围。复用可靠的案例、执行工具与已有结果，明确哪些需要调整、哪些需要补充；区分核实过的事实与设计假设。 按实际风险选择 tests 与 eval，写明每项检查支持什么决定、依赖什么条件。某项条件未满足时，无依赖的工作可以继续；必要的安全检查仍须保留。 需要比较时先确定可信基线 baseline：用户今天的做法，或实际可选的替代方案。 运行前确定验收与停止条件。分别估算环境准备、自动运行和人工审核的工作量；可后置的扩展项写明触发条件。预算用尽时保留部分证据，不等于通过验收。 2 2 · 接通并验证一条运行路径 复用已有基础设施，按已确认方案补齐必要部分。 产出： 可重复运行、评分可信、记录可追溯的检查路径。 搭建已确定的检查 → 具体做法与检查点 准备带版本的案例与合适的数据分区。按标准选择代码、合格人工审核或已验证的模型评分；注明模型评分的验证覆盖哪些标准、任务与决策用途。 接通选定的环节契约、执行器 runner、评分器 grader、结果记录与回放。先用一条较小的完整路径，确认从输入到结果都可检查。 约定权限、预算、外部影响与超时。测量过程损坏或记录不完整时标记运行无效，避免误判产品表现。 3 3 · 运行、分析并做决定 让 Agent 先运行已授权的检查并分析结果。通过决策总览，把人工复核集中在质量判断、业务取舍和需要批准的操作上。 产出： 有依据的建议、重点审核清单与下一步行动。 运行或分析一轮 → 具体做法与检查点 运行已授权的检查，或直接分析已有结果。保留原始输出，比较重要场景，定位行为最早偏离预期的位置。 区分产品失败与测量无效；结合质量、成本、延迟和用户投入，说明不确定性及重要能力是否退步。 每项人工复核请求都附上实际输出、相关输入、判断标准、Agent 分析和一个明确问题。优先审查严重风险、临界结果、评分分歧和新型失败；也抽查部分通过案例，检查是否漏判。记录最终决定及适用范围。 根据职责看结果、做决定 产品 · 把结果与用户影响联系起来，决定下一项产品改动。 工程 · 检查结果能否复现、问题最早出现在哪里，并在约定范围内修复原因。 质量与运营 · 结合真实业务流程审查难判断或高风险的输出，判断是否达到使用要求。 4 4 · 验证真实使用，补充下一轮案例 获准上线后，检查真实用户任务能否保持预期质量与可靠性。 产出： 继续上线、修复或回滚的决定，以及下一版可复用的案例。 分析验证证据 → 产品分析与实验 → 具体做法与检查点 监控错误与延迟，按约定质量标准抽查真实输出。查看表现薄弱的用户群和任务，不只看总体平均值。 按需要与授权使用 影子运行 shadow或 小流量发布 canary。事先设置告警与回滚条件，隔离影子运行的副作用。 把真实失败复核、脱敏后，转成带预期结果的离线案例。修复后重跑相关案例，并保留独立留出集用于后续验证。 想了解采用、完成或留存情况，使用产品分析；想判断改善是否由某项改动引起，使用设计适当的受控实验。"}},{"path":"testing-evaluation-system/testing-evaluation-system.html","anchor":"share","page":{"en":"Testing & Evaluation System","zh":"测试与评估系统"},"title":{"en":"Files and references","zh":"文件结构与参考"},"text":{"en":"Files and references File relationships for this module. Use the workflow sections above for the practical steps. Internal files View this folder on GitHub ↗ Entry README.md Shared file dependencies Task and authority ../_shared/task-contract.md Workflow branches Understand the method 00-testing-evaluation-system.md Design the evidence system 01-design-evidence-system.prompt.md Audit existing evidence 01-audit-existing-system.prompt.md Implement an approved slice 02-implement-approved-system.prompt.md Run or analyze one round 03-run-eval-round.prompt.md Supporting files · read when needed Scope, effort and stopping rules references/bounded-round-design.md For a finite round: acceptance, effort, deferrals and feedback. Comparative design references/comparative-design.md For version, alternative, component or cost comparisons. Robustness and edge cases references/robustness-design.md For relevant input, context or customization variation. Grader selection and combination references/grader-design.md When choosing code, human or model judgment, or validating scores. Agent reliability references/agent-reliability-design.md For stateful tools, authority and recovery. Operational validation references/operational-validation.md Select shadow/canary, load or adversarial sections by risk. Analytics and experiments ../product-analytics-experimentation/README.md For behavior or causal-impact questions. Mermaid file map ↗ How the agent reads these files Choose files by the requested work. A plan loads design, not implementation or a run; an explicit mixed request may use more than one workflow. This package currently starts from the README you give the agent. An installed skill is discovered through its name and description, then its SKILL.md is loaded; references and scripts support the selected task. These maps describe intended reading routes, not a live execution trace or an access-control mechanism. Official skill documentation ↗ External references OpenAI · Evaluation best practices Eval process, evaluator selection and edge cases. LangSmith · Evaluation Datasets, evaluators and experiments. Anthropic · Agent evals Tasks, graders, harnesses and observed outcomes.","zh":"文件结构与参考 本模块的文件关系。具体做法见上方工作流内容。 内部文件 在 GitHub 查看本模块文件夹 ↗ 入口 README.md 共用文件 任务与操作边界 ../_shared/task-contract.md 工作流分支 理解方法 00-testing-evaluation-system.md 设计验证方案 01-design-evidence-system.prompt.md 审查现有体系 01-audit-existing-system.prompt.md 实施已批准的切片 02-implement-approved-system.prompt.md 运行或分析一轮 03-run-eval-round.prompt.md 支持文件 · 按需读取 范围、工作量与停止条件 references/bounded-round-design.md 规划有限一轮时：验收、工作量、后续项与反馈接入。 比较设计 references/comparative-design.md 需要比较版本、替代方案、模块贡献或成本时。 鲁棒性与边界案例 references/robustness-design.md 输入、上下文或定制变化可能影响判断时。 判定方式选择与组合 references/grader-design.md 选择代码、人工或模型判断，或检查分数是否可信时。 Agent 可靠性 references/agent-reliability-design.md 涉及工具、状态、权限与恢复时。 上线与运行验证 references/operational-validation.md 按风险选择影子／灰度、负载或对抗验证章节。 产品分析与实验 ../product-analytics-experimentation/README.md 涉及用户行为或因果影响时读取。 查看 Mermaid 文件图 ↗ Agent 如何读取这些文件 按本轮任务选文件。只做规划时读设计工作流，不进入实施或运行；明确的组合任务可以使用多个工作流。 当前 package 从你交给 Agent 的 README 开始。已安装的 skill 会先通过名称和描述被发现，再读取 SKILL.md，并按任务使用参考文件或脚本。这张图说明预期读取路线，不是实际执行轨迹，也不是权限控制。 官方 skill 说明 ↗ 外部参考 OpenAI · 评估实践 评估流程、判定方式与边界案例。 LangSmith · Evaluation 数据集、评分器与实验。 Anthropic · Agent evals 任务、评分器、harness 与实际结果。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"start","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"text":{"en":"Behavior to decision Product Analytics & Experimentation Observe how people use the product, diagnose friction, and estimate product impact without mixing descriptive evidence with causal claims. Adoption + funnels Retention + cohorts Experiments + causal impact Start from the product decision. First check the data, understand today’s experience, then choose whether an experiment is needed to test a change.","zh":"从行为到决策 产品分析与实验 观察用户如何使用产品、定位摩擦，并在不混淆描述性证据与因果结论的前提下估计产品影响。 采用 + 漏斗 留存 + Cohort 实验 + 因果影响 从产品决策出发。 先核实数据，理解用户当前的体验，再判断是否需要通过实验验证改动。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"position","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"Quality evidence and product evidence run in parallel","zh":"质量证据与产品证据并行运行"},"text":{"en":"Position in product development Quality evidence and product evidence run in parallel Testing & Eval asks whether the system is correct, useful, safe, reliable, and ready. Analytics & Experiments asks what users do, where the workflow breaks down, and whether a product change caused a meaningful outcome. Testing & Eval Correctness · output quality · safety · reliability · release readiness Combined product decision Analytics & Experiments Behavior · friction · retention · cohorts · causal product impact Product question State what you need to decide. Measurement definitions Agree on who and what to count. Current experience See how people use the product today. Hypothesis Suggest why a problem occurs and what might help. Experiment Test whether a change caused an improvement. Rollout + follow-up Monitor real use and update the decision record.","zh":"在产品开发中的位置 质量证据与产品证据并行运行 测试与评估判断系统是否正确、好用、安全、可靠并具备发布条件；产品分析与实验判断用户如何行动、流程在哪里受阻，以及产品改动是否造成了有意义的结果。 测试与评估 正确性 · 输出质量 · 安全 · 可靠性 · 发布准备度 综合产品决策 产品分析与实验 行为 · 摩擦 · 留存 · Cohort · 产品因果影响 产品问题 明确接下来要做什么决定。 统一统计口径 约定统计谁、记录什么、怎么算。 了解当前体验 观察用户现在如何使用产品。 产品假设 提出问题的可能原因和改善方案。 实验 验证改善是否由这项改动造成。 发布 + 后续验证 持续观察真实使用并更新决策记录。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"choose","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"Start with the question you need to answer","zh":"从你需要回答的问题开始"},"text":{"en":"Choose the work mode Start with the question you need to answer The agent can choose the route from your question. Each mode produces something the next step can reuse. Work mode Your question What happens What you get Measurement design Can we trust the numbers we need? Define who counts, what action is recorded, and how the metric is calculated. A shared definition and a plan to fill data gaps. Behavior analysis Where do people stop, return, or need extra effort? Trace the workflow and compare groups or periods to locate a problem and propose explanations. A finding, supporting evidence, and the next investigation. Experiment design How can we tell whether this change helps? Plan who receives A or B, what improvement matters, and when to continue or stop. A written plan agreed before the experiment starts. Experiment analysis Did the change help enough to act on? Check the experiment ran as planned, then estimate improvement and any harmful effects. A supported rollout, iteration, or follow-up decision.","zh":"选择工作模式 从你需要回答的问题开始 Agent 可以根据你的问题选择路径。每一种模式都有明确产出，供后续工作继续使用。 工作模式 你的问题 会做什么 得到什么 设计数据记录与指标 需要的数字能否被可靠统计？ 明确统计谁、记录什么行为、指标怎么算。 统一的口径，以及补齐缺失数据的方案。 理解用户行为 用户在哪停下、是否回来、哪里很费力？ 沿流程定位问题，比较人群与时期，提出可能的原因。 发现、支持证据与下一步调查。 设计产品实验 如何判断这项改动是否有帮助？ 规划谁使用 A / B、什么改善值得关注、何时继续或停止。 实验开始前确定的完整计划。 解读实验结果 改动是否产生了值得行动的改善？ 先核实实验按计划运行，再估计改善程度与可能的负面影响。 有证据支持的发布、迭代或后续验证决策。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"foundation","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"Understand how the numbers are produced","zh":"先看清数字是怎么得来的"},"text":{"en":"Measurement foundation Understand how the numbers are produced A product metric connects three things: who used the product, what they did, and how the result is counted. Check that chain before treating a change in the chart as a change in the product. 01 · Identity Who are we counting? Recognize the same person across visits or devices; use an account as the unit when the product serves a team. Example: one person using a phone and a laptop still counts as one user. 02 · Events What actually happened? An event records an action at a defined moment. A click on Save and a successful save are different events. Example: count success only after the document has been saved. 03 · Metrics How is the result counted? Turn events into a number using a consistent population, formula, and time window. Example: of 100 users who started a draft this week, 40 saved it within seven days: 40% completion. Then interpret the result Compare periods or cohorts (groups defined by a shared condition) using the same metric definition, then decide what to investigate or improve. Why verify this first? A broken success event can make completion appear to fall. Duplicate events can inflate an event-count metric. Both can change the chart while the actual experience stays the same. Implementation details: what to check at each step Identity — avoid splitting or merging people incorrectly Link anonymous activity to the correct signed-in user. Define how multiple people belong to a shared account or workspace, and how deletion affects reporting. Events — make the record match the action Verify the trigger, required information, success/failure distinction, timestamps, and duplicate handling. Compare a few known actions with their stored records. Metrics — make comparisons use the same definition Check the counted unit, numerator, denominator, time window, and exclusions. Confirm the dashboard and source query return the same result. A measurement contract is the written agreement for these definitions: what counts, how it is recorded, how it is calculated, and which version the analysis uses. Cohort, time cohort, and experiment assignment Cohort · a group defined by a shared condition For example, users who signed up in the same week, or users who saved at least one draft last month. Reuse the definition when comparing behavior or tracking return visits. Time cohort · grouped by a shared starting period For example, compare users who signed up in week 1 and week 2 at the same point after signup. This makes retention comparisons fairer. Experiment assignment · deciding who receives A or B Among eligible participants, assign users or accounts to variants according to the experiment design. Bucketing is a technical mechanism for making that assignment repeatable; with stable inputs and configuration, the same unit keeps its group. Example: users who signed up this week → Select this cohort as the eligible population → Randomly assign participants to A or B → Record which experience each participant actually encountered If the treatment can change cohort membership, comparing only members after the experiment can bias the result. Define the experiment population and analysis plan before launch. In an experiment: assignment and exposure are separate records Assignment means the system selected a variant for someone. Exposure means they reached the defined point where that variant could affect their experience. A user assigned to a new editor may never open it. Keep both records. The primary analysis often follows the original assignment; an exposed-user analysis needs a pre-defined rule because opening the feature may itself be affected by the treatment.","zh":"数据如何变成指标 先看清数字是怎么得来的 一个产品指标需要连接三件事：谁在使用、做了什么、结果怎么算。先确认这条链记录和计算准确，才能判断图表变化是否反映了产品变化。 01 · 用户识别 统计的是谁？ 识别跨访问、跨设备的同一个人；团队产品也可能按账户而不是个人统计。 例：同一个人用手机和电脑登录，仍算一名用户。 02 · 行为记录 实际发生了什么？ Event 是在明确时点记录的一次行为。点击“保存”和“保存成功”应分别记录。 例：文档真正保存完成后，才记录“保存成功”。 03 · 指标计算 结果怎么算？ 用一致的统计人群、计算公式和时间范围，把行为记录变成指标。 例：本周开始写草稿的 100 人中，40 人在七天内保存成功，完成率为 40%。 再解释这个结果 用相同口径比较不同时期或 同期群 cohort，即按共同条件定义的人群，再决定调查什么、改进什么。 为什么先核实这条链？ “保存成功”事件漏记，会让完成率看起来下降；事件重复上报，会把按次数统计的指标抬高。图表变化可能来自记录问题，而非体验变化。 实施细节：每一步检查什么 用户识别：避免把一个人拆开，或把不同人合并 把匿名访问关联到正确的登录用户；明确多人共用账户或 团队工作空间 workspace时如何统计，以及删除数据后如何处理报表。 行为记录：让数据对应真实动作 核实触发时点、必填信息、成功与失败的区别、时间戳和去重规则；实际操作几次，确认保存的记录与操作一致。 指标计算：让比较使用相同口径 检查按人还是按次统计、分子、分母、时间范围和排除规则；确认 Dashboard 与底层查询的结果一致。 衡量约定 measurement contract就是把这些口径写清楚：什么算数、如何记录、如何计算，以及本次分析使用哪个版本。 Cohort、同期群与实验分组 Cohort · 按共同条件定义的人群 例如“同一周注册的用户”，或“上个月至少保存过一次草稿的用户”。用同一组定义比较行为，或观察这些人之后是否回来。 同期群 · 按共同起始时期定义的 Cohort 例如比较第一周与第二周注册的人，在各自注册七天后的留存。“同期群”在这种以时间定义的场景最直观。 实验分组 · 决定谁使用 A 或 B 在符合条件的参与者中，按实验设计把用户或账户分配给不同方案。“分桶 bucketing”是实现可重复分配的技术机制；标识与配置不变时，同一单位保持在同一组。 例：本周注册的用户 → 选择这个 Cohort 作为实验人群 → 在其中随机分配 A / B → 记录每个人实际接触了哪个方案 如果产品改动本身会影响谁进入 Cohort，实验后只比较这些成员可能让结果偏差。实验人群与分析方式应在开始前确定。 做实验时：分组与实际接触要分别记录 分组是系统决定给某人哪个版本；实际接触 exposure，常译“曝光”是他到达了该版本能够影响体验的时点。被分配到新版编辑器的用户，可能根本没有打开编辑器。 两种记录都要保留。主要分析通常按最初分组进行；只分析实际接触者时，需要预先定义规则，因为是否打开功能本身也可能受到改动影响。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"analysis","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"Use the workflow to locate the question","zh":"沿着用户流程找到问题"},"text":{"en":"Behavior analysis Use the workflow to locate the question These views answer different questions about the same experience. Start with the view closest to the product decision. Start Adoption + activation Adoption asks who starts using the feature. Activation asks who reaches its first meaningful result, such as saving a usable draft. Complete Funnel Track how many people reach each step: open editor → generate → save. A large drop identifies a step to investigate. Return Retention + cohort Follow a defined group over time. For example, how many of this week’s new users return to complete a task next week? Effort Journey + effort Inspect the route to completion: how often do people retry, edit, or backtrack, and how long does it take? Investigate Choose the next evidence Use the pattern to decide whether to interview users, inspect quality, repair data, or test a product change. Example: many users generate a draft, but few save it First confirm the save event is recorded correctly. Then locate the drop between generation and saving, and compare new and returning users using consistent definitions. Several explanations remain possible: weak output, a hard-to-find save button, or no intention to save. Review sample outputs and user sessions or interview users before selecting a change to test. A funnel locates the drop; it does not identify the cause on its own. A controlled experiment can then estimate whether the proposed change improves completion.","zh":"理解用户行为 沿着用户流程找到问题 这些视角从不同方面解释同一次使用体验。先选择最接近当前产品决策的视角。 开始使用 采用 + 激活 采用关注谁开始使用；激活关注谁第一次获得有意义的结果，例如保存了一份可用草稿。 完成流程 漏斗 看每一步还有多少人：打开编辑器 → 生成 → 保存。人数明显减少的步骤值得进一步调查。 再次使用 留存 + Cohort 持续观察一组定义明确的人。例如本周新用户中，有多少人下周再次回来完成任务？ 使用投入 路径 + 投入 查看完成任务的实际路径：重试几次、修改多少、是否来回操作，以及花了多久。 继续调查 选择下一步证据 根据发现，决定访谈用户、检查输出质量、修复数据，或实验一项产品改动。 例子：很多人生成了草稿，却很少保存 先确认“保存”事件记录准确，再定位“生成 → 保存”之间的流失，并按一致口径比较新用户与老用户。 可能的解释包括：输出不好、保存按钮难找，或用户本来就不需要保存。可以抽查输出、观察使用过程或访谈用户，再决定要验证哪项改动。 漏斗帮助定位流失，但不能单凭它确定原因。之后可以通过受控实验估计改动是否提高完成率。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"experiment","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"Plan how to tell whether a change helps","zh":"先计划如何判断改动是否有效"},"text":{"en":"Controlled experimentation Plan how to tell whether a change helps An A/B experiment randomly assigns eligible participants to two experiences and compares the results. For example, test whether a clearer save button improves draft completion while error rate stays acceptable. 01 · Plan What changes, and for whom? State the hypothesis, define eligible participants, and assign them to the current experience A or changed experience B. Design details: population and assignment Choose an assignment unit: a person, account, or workspace. Keep a whole team in one group when teammates could affect one another. Record the intended difference between A and B, the proposed mechanism, and actual exposure. Check that participants do not accidentally receive both variants. 02 · Measure What improvement matters? Choose one main outcome, such as task completion, and guardrails for things that must remain acceptable, such as errors or cost. Design details: effect size and sample Baseline is the current level. Practical significance is the smallest improvement worth the effort. MDE is the effect size the experiment is designed to detect with its chosen sample and statistical power. Statistical power describes the chance of detecting an effect of that size if it exists. Estimate sample size and duration from the baseline, variation, MDE, and chosen error rates. 03 · Decide When is there enough evidence? Agree on duration, analysis, and stopping rules in advance. Review the estimated effect and its uncertainty before expanding or revising the change. Analysis details: validity and uncertainty SRM (sample-ratio mismatch) means the observed group sizes differ unexpectedly from the planned split. Investigate assignment or logging problems before interpreting impact. An uncertainty interval shows how precise the effect estimate is. Check guardrails, respect the planned stopping rule, and label unplanned subgroup analyses as exploratory. Possible next steps Expand the rollout Revise and retest Keep the current version Fix data or gather more evidence When A/A, canary, or shadow is useful A/A · check the experiment setup Give both groups the same experience to check randomization, records, and analysis. One non-significant result alone does not prove the setup is reliable. Canary · release to a small share first Watch errors, quality, and other limits while limiting exposure. Expand gradually or roll back; causal attribution still requires an appropriate experiment design. Shadow · run alongside the live version Process mirrored real inputs without serving the candidate result or executing its external actions. Compare outputs safely before giving the candidate production responsibility.","zh":"受控实验 先计划如何判断改动是否有效 A/B 实验把符合条件的参与者随机分配到两个体验，再比较结果。例如验证更清晰的保存按钮能否提高草稿完成率，同时保持可接受的错误率。 01 · 定义实验 改变什么，影响谁？ 说明产品假设，确定参与人群，再将其分配到当前体验 A 或改动体验 B。 设计细节：参与人群与分组 明确按个人、账户还是 Workspace 分组。如果团队成员会相互影响，应考虑让整个团队处于同一组。 记录 A / B 的预期差异、改动为什么可能有效，以及实际接触情况；检查用户是否意外接触了两个版本。 02 · 衡量结果 什么改善值得关注？ 选择一个主要结果，例如任务完成率；同时设置防护指标，确保错误率或成本等仍可接受。 设计细节：效果大小与样本 Baseline 是当前水平；实际意义指多大的改善值得投入；最小可检测效果（MDE）指实验在给定样本量和统计功效下计划识别的效果大小。 统计功效表示：如果确实存在这么大的效果，实验有多大概率识别出来。根据当前水平、波动、MDE 与设定的错误率，估计需要多少样本和多长时间。 03 · 做出判断 什么时候证据足够？ 提前约定时长、分析和停止规则。查看估计的效果及不确定性，再决定扩大范围或继续修改。 分析细节：有效性与不确定性 样本比例异常（SRM）指实际组人数与计划比例出现异常差异。先排查分组或记录问题，再解释产品效果。 不确定性区间帮助判断效果估计有多精确。审查防护指标，遵守预先约定的停止规则，并把临时追加的分群分析标为探索性发现。 可能的下一步 扩大发布范围 修改后重新实验 保留当前版本 修复数据或补充证据 什么时候用 A/A、Canary 或影子验证 A/A · 检查实验系统 让两组使用相同体验，检查分组、记录与分析是否可靠。仅一次结果“没有显著差异”，还不足以证明系统完全可靠。 Canary · 先让少量流量使用新版本 先观察错误率、质量等指标，控制潜在影响范围，再逐步放量或回滚。若要判断因果影响，仍需合适的实验设计。 影子验证 · 与线上版本并行运行 候选版本处理镜像的真实输入，但不向用户提供结果，也不执行对外动作。先比较输出，再决定是否让它承担线上职责。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"evidence","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"AI quality and product outcomes meet at the decision","zh":"AI 质量与产品结果在决策处汇合"},"text":{"en":"Connected evidence AI quality and product outcomes meet at the decision A better offline score does not automatically improve user behavior, and higher usage does not prove output quality. Preserve each claim type, then join them with shared release, variant, and trace identifiers. Offline eval Pre-release quality, comparison, and regression evidence on curated or historical cases. Online eval + monitoring Live quality, safety, reliability, drift, incidents, cost, and latency. Product analytics Observed behavior, effort, adoption, conversion, retention, and association. Controlled experiment Causal impact within the experiment's population, treatment, duration, and validity assumptions. Useful shared signals: latency, cost, retries, human correction effort, acceptance, override, abandonment, task completion, and incident rate.","zh":"连接证据 AI 质量与产品结果在决策处汇合 更高的离线得分不会自动改善用户行为，更高的使用量也不能证明输出质量。保留每种证据的结论边界，再通过共享的版本、实验方案与 Trace 标识连接起来。 离线 Eval 基于精选或历史案例的发布前质量、比较与回归证据。 在线 Eval + 监控 线上质量、安全、可靠性、漂移、事故、成本与延迟。 产品分析 观察到的行为、投入、采用、转化、留存与相关关系。 受控实验 在实验人群、方案、时长与有效性假设范围内的因果影响。 适合跨体系连接的信号： 延迟、成本、重试、人工修改投入、接受、覆盖、放弃、任务完成与事故率。"}},{"path":"product-analytics-experimentation/product-analytics-experimentation.html","anchor":"route","page":{"en":"Product Analytics & Experimentation","zh":"产品分析与实验"},"title":{"en":"Files and references","zh":"文件结构与参考"},"text":{"en":"Files and references File relationships for this module. Use the workflow sections above for the practical steps. Internal files View this folder on GitHub ↗ Entry README.md Shared file dependencies Task and authority ../_shared/task-contract.md Workflow file · select a mode within it Product evidence workflow 01-product-evidence-workflow.prompt.md Supporting files · read when needed Method and contracts 00-product-analytics-experimentation.md Read relevant definitions and analysis rules as needed. Testing and eval ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md For concrete quality, reliability or comparative measurement. Mermaid file map ↗ How the agent reads these files Five modes share one workflow file. The mode controls which work is performed, not whether the other mode descriptions enter context. This package currently starts from the README you give the agent. An installed skill is discovered through its name and description, then its SKILL.md is loaded; references and scripts support the selected task. These maps describe intended reading routes, not a live execution trace or an access-control mechanism. Official skill documentation ↗ External references Amplitude · Analytics Product behavior analysis. Amplitude · Experiment Controlled experimentation. Cohort definitions Group users by shared properties or behavior. Sticky bucketing Keep experiment assignments consistent.","zh":"文件结构与参考 本模块的文件关系。具体做法见上方工作流内容。 内部文件 在 GitHub 查看本模块文件夹 ↗ 入口 README.md 共用文件 任务与操作边界 ../_shared/task-contract.md 工作流文件 · 在文件内选择模式 产品证据工作流 01-product-evidence-workflow.prompt.md 支持文件 · 按需读取 方法与契约 00-product-analytics-experimentation.md 按需查阅定义、契约与分析规则。 测试与评估 ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md 需要具体质量、可靠性或对照衡量方案时读取。 查看 Mermaid 文件图 ↗ Agent 如何读取这些文件 五个模式共用一个工作流文件。模式选择决定执行哪项工作，不意味着其他模式的说明完全不进入上下文。 当前 package 从你交给 Agent 的 README 开始。已安装的 skill 会先通过名称和描述被发现，再读取 SKILL.md，并按任务使用参考文件或脚本。这张图说明预期读取路线，不是实际执行轨迹，也不是权限控制。 官方 skill 说明 ↗ 外部参考 Amplitude · Analytics 产品行为分析。 Amplitude · Experiment 受控实验。 Cohort 定义 按共同属性或行为定义用户群。 稳定分桶 保持实验分配一致。"}},{"path":"delivery-learning/delivery-learning.html","anchor":"start","page":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"title":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"text":{"en":"Draft 0.1 Delivery & Learning Turn an approved direction into a verified change and a clear next decision. Deliver one useful path, preserve evidence, and learn from what actually happens.","zh":"初稿 0.1 交付与学习 把已批准方向做成可验证的改动，并明确下一决定。 交付一条有用路径，保留证据，从实际发生的结果中学习。"}},{"path":"delivery-learning/delivery-learning.html","anchor":"path","page":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"title":{"en":"Move from approval to evidence","zh":"从批准走向证据"},"text":{"en":"Move from approval to evidence Deliver a bounded user outcome through the real execution path. Keep implementation, release authority, and acceptance separate so progress remains verifiable. Approved direction Outcome and change boundary. Structural slice A complete, narrow path. Verification Tests, evals, and read-back. Release and learn Authorized exposure and feedback. Status dimension Example states What establishes it Decision Proposed → approved → superseded. An accountable decision and a named scope/version. Delivery Local implementation → integration → deployment. Code, artifact, environment, and release record. Verification Unchecked → checked in an environment → live observation → user acceptance. Actual checks and artifacts; acceptance by the accountable user. Authority at each step An approved design permits the agreed next phase. Paid calls, production migration, deployment, and external communication need their own authorization.","zh":"从批准走向证据 沿真实执行路径交付范围明确的用户结果。区分实现、上线授权与验收，让进度可以核实。 已批准方向 结果与改动边界。 结构性切片 范围小、路径完整。 验证 测试、eval 与回读。 上线与学习 获批上线与反馈。 状态维度 示例状态 如何确认 决定 提议 → 已批准 → 被新决定替代。 责任明确的决定，以及指定范围和版本。 交付 本地实现 → 集成 → 部署。 代码、产物、环境与发布记录。 验证 未检查 → 环境内验证 → 线上观察 → 用户验收。 实际检查与产物，以及责任用户的验收。 每一步的授权 设计获批后进入约定的下一阶段。付费调用、生产迁移、部署和外部沟通仍需各自的授权。"}},{"path":"delivery-learning/delivery-learning.html","anchor":"slice","page":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"title":{"en":"Define a verifiable slice","zh":"定义可验证的切片"},"text":{"en":"Define a verifiable slice A structural slice crosses enough of the system to complete one user task. Its acceptance criteria include results, failure behavior, and recovery. Specify Purpose Required content Outcome and boundary Keep work aligned with the approved promise. User job, included behavior, approval reference, preserved behavior. Contracts and dependencies Make independently built parts compatible. Inputs/outputs, source ownership, producers/consumers, version and errors. Acceptance and recovery Show what completion means and how failure is contained. Tests/eval criteria, read-back, rollback, partial and ambiguous states. Owner and handoff Make the next action clear. Implementer, reviewer, release/incident owner, evidence links. Risk gate · what to validate before expanding work Find the assumption whose failure would invalidate downstream work: data access, provider capability, output quality, authority, compatibility, or operating cost. Define the evidence, budget, owner, and consequence before the check.","zh":"定义可验证的切片 结构性切片跨越完成一个用户任务所需的系统环节。验收标准同时覆盖结果、失败行为与恢复。 需要明确 用途 具体内容 结果与边界 让工作对应已批准的用户承诺。 用户任务、包含行为、批准依据与保持不变的行为。 契约与依赖 让不同部分能够正确接合。 输入输出、来源归属、生产者与消费者、版本与错误。 验收与恢复 说明什么算完成，以及如何控制失败。 测试与 eval 标准、回读、回滚、部分和不明确状态。 负责人与交接 让下一步有明确归属。 实现、审核、上线与事故负责人，以及证据链接。 风险门槛 · 扩大工作前先验证什么 找出一旦失败就会使后续工作失效的假设：数据访问、供应商能力、输出质量、权限、兼容性或运行成本。验证前写清证据、预算、负责人和失败后如何调整方向。"}},{"path":"delivery-learning/delivery-learning.html","anchor":"boundaries","page":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"title":{"en":"Check system boundaries","zh":"检查系统边界"},"text":{"en":"Check system boundaries Reuse explicit contracts and verify that each capability is actually wired. For AI products, the harness joins instructions, context, models, tools, state, and controls into a working system. Schema and contract A schema defines data shape and meaning. A contract adds behavioral promises: ownership, permissions, errors, compatibility, and what happens across the boundary. Wiring and removability A file or feature flag is only part of the evidence. Verify the reachable path, consumer, execution, and what happens when the capability is disabled. Contract checklist · data, state, errors, and change Boundary What to specify Verification Data meaning Required/optional/null/default, IDs, tenant, units, time, provenance. Runtime validation against representative and malformed inputs. State and authority Allowed transitions, actor, approval, side effects, concurrency. Permission, duplicate-action, and state-transition checks. Failure and recovery Retryable/permanent/partial errors, timeout, idempotency, read-back. Fault injection, interrupted runs, and reconciliation checks. Change ownership Producer/consumer, schema version, compatibility, migration, retirement. Consumer contract tests and migration/rollback evidence. AI harness and removal drill Trace prompt/context assembly, model routing, tool permissions, memory scope, validation, approval, persistence, and delivery. Keep versioned traces of material inputs, stage outputs, configuration, latency, cost, and final disposition with privacy controls. For removal, inspect UI, prompts, registries, events, jobs, stored data, consumers, telemetry, and eval cases. Distinguish disable, deprecate, and delete. Verify disabled behavior stops executing and incurring cost; plan migration and rollback for active consumers. Start with a paper drill in review mode. Execute removal only after approval of the specific scope.","zh":"检查系统边界 复用明确契约，验证能力是否真正接入。AI 产品中的 harness 把指令、上下文、模型、工具、状态和控制连接成可工作的系统。 Schema 与 contract Schema 定义数据形状与含义；contract 还包括行为承诺：归属、权限、错误、兼容性，以及跨边界时发生什么。 接入与可移除性 文件或 feature flag 只是部分证据。核实可达路径、消费者、执行，以及关闭能力后的实际行为。 契约检查表 · 数据、状态、错误与变更 边界 需要明确 验证方式 数据含义 必填、可选、空值、默认值、ID、租户、单位、时间与来源。 用代表性和异常输入验证运行时校验。 状态与权限 允许的状态转换、操作者、批准、副作用与并发。 权限、重复操作与状态转换检查。 失败与恢复 可重试、永久与部分错误，超时、幂等和回读。 故障注入、中断运行与核对恢复检查。 变更归属 生产者与消费者、schema 版本、兼容、迁移与退役。 消费者契约测试，以及迁移与回滚证据。 AI harness 与移除演练 追踪 prompt 与上下文组装、模型路由、工具权限、记忆范围、验证、批准、持久化与交付。 在隐私控制下记录重要输入、环节输出、配置、延迟、成本和最终处理结果的版本化 trace。 移除时检查 UI、prompt、注册表、事件、任务、存量数据、消费者、遥测和 eval 案例。 区分临时关闭、弃用迁移与删除。验证关闭后不再执行或产生费用，为活跃消费者规划迁移与回滚。 审查模式先做纸面演练；具体范围获批后才执行移除。"}},{"path":"delivery-learning/delivery-learning.html","anchor":"readiness","page":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"title":{"en":"Review release readiness","zh":"审查上线准备"},"text":{"en":"Review release readiness Combine evidence with operating controls. The decision to expose a change depends on risk, reversibility, and whether important failures can be detected and contained. Check Evidence required Decision Correctness and quality Relevant tests, eval results, artifact versions, and reviewed residual risk. Ready, blocked, or needs targeted review. Compatibility and recovery Migration, old/new consumers, read-back, rollback limits. Proceed with a recovery plan or resolve a blocking dependency. Exposure and operations Eligibility, monitoring, stop conditions, responsible owner. Use the authorized rollout and decide whether to expand. Rollout reference · flags, shadow, and canary A flag controls eligibility; a kill switch stops a capability. Shadow can run a candidate without applying its outputs; canary exposes a limited share to the new version. Define side-effect isolation, comparison conditions, observation windows, and rollback gates for the actual system. A rollout check supports an operational decision. Use an appropriate experimental design when the question is causal product impact.","zh":"审查上线准备 把验证证据与运行控制结合起来。是否上线取决于风险、可逆性，以及能否发现和控制重要失败。 检查 需要的证据 支持的决定 正确性与质量 相关测试、eval 结果、产物版本与已审阅的剩余风险。 就绪、阻塞或需要专项审核。 兼容与恢复 迁移、新旧消费者、回读与回滚限制。 带恢复方案推进，或先解决阻塞依赖。 上线范围与运行 上线对象、监控、停止条件与负责人。 按授权计划上线，并判断是否扩大。 上线参考 · Flag、shadow 与 canary Flag 控制启用对象，kill switch 用于停止能力。Shadow 可运行候选版本但不执行其输出；canary 让有限流量实际使用新版本。需要为具体系统定义副作用隔离、比较条件、观察窗口和回滚门槛。 上线检查支持运行决策；要判断产品因果影响时，使用合适的实验设计。"}},{"path":"delivery-learning/delivery-learning.html","anchor":"learning","page":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"title":{"en":"Turn outcomes into the next improvement","zh":"把结果转成下一次改进"},"text":{"en":"Turn outcomes into the next improvement Inspect what happened before deciding what it means. Link the observed version, population, window, and artifacts to every proposed change. Observe Quality, behavior, incidents, effort, cost. Explain Find patterns and competing explanations. Decide Keep, iterate, expand, pause, retire. Update Cases, contracts, product assumptions. Agent analyzes first Locate failures, compare versions, summarize uncertainty, and attach actual outputs to a focused review queue. People own consequential judgment Review hard-limit failures, ambiguous results, trade-offs, and acceptance. Make the next decision explicit and evidence-linked. One reusable handoff Outcome, approved scope, and separate decision/delivery/verification statuses. Commit, environment, changed files, contract impact, and evidence links. Commands actually run, results, and checks not performed. Rollout controls, migration, rollback limits, owner, and unresolved risks. The next bounded action and the specific decision needed from a person.","zh":"把结果转成下一次改进 先检查发生了什么，再判断它意味着什么。每项改进建议都对应观察版本、人群、时间窗口与产物。 观察 质量、行为、事故、投入与成本。 解释 识别模式与其他可能解释。 决定 保留、迭代、扩大、暂停、退役。 更新 案例、契约与产品假设。 Agent 先分析 定位失败、比较版本、归纳不确定性，把实际输出附到重点审核队列。 人负责重要判断 审查硬性限制失败、不明确结果、取舍与验收，形成明确且可追溯的下一决定。 一份可继续工作的交接 结果、已批准范围，以及分开的决定、交付和验证状态。 提交、环境、改动文件、契约影响与证据链接。 实际运行的命令、结果与未执行检查。 上线控制、迁移、回滚限制、负责人和未解决风险。 下一项有限行动，以及需要人作出的具体决定。"}},{"path":"delivery-learning/delivery-learning.html","anchor":"files","page":{"en":"Delivery & Learning","zh":"交付与学习"},"title":{"en":"Files and references","zh":"文件结构与参考"},"text":{"en":"Files and references File relationships for this module. Use the workflow sections above for the practical steps. Internal files View this folder on GitHub ↗ Entry README.md Shared file dependencies Task and authority ../_shared/task-contract.md Workflow file · select a mode within it Delivery workflow 01-delivery-learning.prompt.md Supporting files · read when needed AI system audit ../ai-product-system-audit/README.md For material wiring, harness or contract uncertainty. Testing and eval ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md For concrete quality, reliability or comparative measurement. Analytics and experiments ../product-analytics-experimentation/README.md For behavior or causal-impact questions. Shared restructuring method ( EN / 简中 ) ../product-ux-rethinking/00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md For deeper evidence, responsibility or structural questions. Context update discipline ../context-update-discipline/README.md When feedback changes the current scope or intent. Mermaid file map ↗ How the agent reads these files One file contains slice planning, approved implementation, readiness review and learning review. Apply only the requested mode within its authority. This package currently starts from the README you give the agent. An installed skill is discovered through its name and description, then its SKILL.md is loaded; references and scripts support the selected task. These maps describe intended reading routes, not a live execution trace or an access-control mechanism. Official skill documentation ↗ External references Google SRE · Canarying releases Bounded exposure, monitoring and rollback.","zh":"文件结构与参考 本模块的文件关系。具体做法见上方工作流内容。 内部文件 在 GitHub 查看本模块文件夹 ↗ 入口 README.md 共用文件 任务与操作边界 ../_shared/task-contract.md 工作流文件 · 在文件内选择模式 交付工作流 01-delivery-learning.prompt.md 支持文件 · 按需读取 AI 系统审查 ../ai-product-system-audit/README.md 接入、harness 或契约存在关键不确定性时读取。 测试与评估 ../testing-evaluation-system/README.md 需要具体质量、可靠性或对照衡量方案时读取。 产品分析与实验 ../product-analytics-experimentation/README.md 涉及用户行为或因果影响时读取。 通用重构方法 ( EN / 简中 ) ../product-ux-rethinking/00-general-product-restructuring-workflow.en.md 需要深入处理证据、责任或结构问题时读取。 上下文更新规范 ../context-update-discipline/README.md 反馈改变当前范围或意图时读取。 查看 Mermaid 文件图 ↗ Agent 如何读取这些文件 一个文件包含切片规划、获批实施、就绪审查和学习复盘；只执行本轮要求且获授权的模式。 当前 package 从你交给 Agent 的 README 开始。已安装的 skill 会先通过名称和描述被发现，再读取 SKILL.md，并按任务使用参考文件或脚本。这张图说明预期读取路线，不是实际执行轨迹，也不是权限控制。 官方 skill 说明 ↗ 外部参考 Google SRE · 灰度发布 受控放量、监控与回滚。"}}];
